xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2019-06-17T08:47:07"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aerial views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "glossary (Bird's-eye view. A perspective representation of the landscape, as it might be visible from a high viewpoint above the surface of the Earth, or other celestial body, in which detail is shown as if projected on to an oblique plane. See also View.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Descriptive cataloging of rare materials (cartographic), 2016:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Glossary of the mapping sciences, 1994;Cartographic materials, 2002, 2005 update", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "aerial views (aerial views. UF air views. SN Refers to views achieved by photographing from an aircraft or other high location, or in any medium imagined as if seen from such a high location. When emphasizing a photograph itself, use \"aerial photographs.\" For nonphotographic depictions having high viewpoints, typically prefer \"bird's-eye views\" or \"bird's-eye perspectives.\") bird's-eye views (bird's-eye views. UF balloon views. SN Refers to nonphotographic depictions having a viewpoint well above normal eye level. They are typically prints, drawings or paintings that incorporate a point of view as if the viewer were looking at the ground from the level of the clouds. The advantage of the high angle is that more detail can be displayed, as the foreground does not obscure the background. This view has been used since the time of ancient Rome, when it was used to portray battlefields; it is also commonly used to portray urban developments, for landscape garden plans, and for palaces and towns. Bird's-eye views depict a vantage point higher than one taken from just above roof-level, but lower than a map-view. For architectural drawings in precise perspective, use \"bird's-eye perspectives.\" For photographs, use \"aerial views\" or \"aerial photographs.\" For pictorial maps, use \"map views.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Art & architecture thesaurus online, Apr. 20, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Brown's Lend & Engineering Co. Birds eye view of Everett Washington, 1893, 1983.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "glossary (Bird's-eye view. A perspective representation of the landscape, as it might be visible from a high viewpoint above the surface of the Earth, or other celestial body, in which detail is shown as if projected on to an oblique plane. See also View (Cartography))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cartographic materials, 2003, 2005 update:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Bird's-eye view; aerial view; Overhead view is fairly synonymous with bird's-eye view)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Sept. 15, 2010", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aerial views (Aerial views. UF Air views, Balloon views. SN Views from a high vantage point. BT Views. NT Aerial photographs. RT Bird's-eye views, Panoramic views) Bird's-eye views (Bird's-eye views. UF Balloon views. SN Graphic representations of scenes portrayed as if viewed from above at an oblique angle. If of a city or town, not generally drawn strictly to scale, they show street patterns, individual buildings, and major landscape features in perspective. BT Views. RT Aerial views, Maps, Panoramic views, Projections)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Thesaurus for graphic materials, via WWW, Apr. 20, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Views--Aerial (A perspective representation of cities or landscapes portrayed as if viewed from above at an oblique angle; not generally drawn to scale but shows street patterns, individual buildings, and major landscape features (e.g., bird's-eye view, panorama, panoramic drawing, worm's-eye view))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Form/genre for cartographic materials [draft of LC working group], 1996:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Balloon views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Balloon views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Overhead views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Overhead views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b19", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b20"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Air views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b20", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Air views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b22", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b23"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bird's-eye views"}}, {"@id": "_:na2b72cd1bc13483bb658ea758c9f1868b23", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bird's-eye views"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026033"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026034", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aAeronautical charts", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026034", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b1"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aeronautical charts"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026387"}, "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026055"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026374"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026449"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b5"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b6"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b7"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b8"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b10"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Maps giving information intended for use in air navigation, such as compass rose, isogonic lines, location of landing fields, beacons, hazards to air navigation, etc.", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009025062"}}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-01T14:35:53"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aeronautical charts"}}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "chart, aeronautical (a chart designed for use in navigating aircraft. An aeronautical chart shows airports and aids to and hazards to aerial navigation, as well as some of the natural features an man-made objects shown on general maps. Also called a navigational chart)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Glossary of the mapping sciences, 1994:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(hdg.: Aeronautical charts)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, Dec. 1, 2009:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(aeronautical chart: map designed to assist in navigation of aircraft, much as nautical charts do for watercraft, or a roadmap for drivers)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Dec. 1, 2009:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(aeronautical chart: a specialized representation of mapped features of the earth, or some part of it, produced to show selected terrain, cultural and hydrographic features, and supplemental information required for air navigation, pilotage, or for planning air operations)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Glossary of mapping, charting, and geodetic terms, 1973:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Credo reference, Dec. 1, 2009.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Navigational charts"}}, {"@id": "_:n1ad94efc74f14e4b88abfe6d25705864b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Navigational charts"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026034"}
