or events are depicted under invented names see [Films \u00e0 clef.]", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007025024"}}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-08-11T17:29:02"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Biographical films"}}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Biographical film (Bio, Biog, Biography, Biopic, Film biography, Screen biography))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "L\u00f3pez, D. Films by genre, c1993", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 241 (biographic films on sport heroines)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Sexual sports rhetoric, \u00a92010:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Film genres > Film sub-genres > Biopics (Biopics Films; Biopic films (or biographical pictures) are a sub-genre of the larger drama and epic film genres, and although they reached a hey-day of popularity in the 1930s, they are still prominent to this day; biopics; biographical epics)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Filmsite.org, Mar. 16, 2012:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cones, J.W. Motion picture biographies, c1997.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 42 (biographic films)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Min, E. Korean film, 2003:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(biopics)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Custen, G.F. Biographical movies, 1992", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(A biographical film, or biopic (biographical motion picture), is a film that dramatizes the life of an actual person or people. They differ from films \"based on a true story\" or \"historical films\" in that they attempt to comprehensively tell a person's life story or at least the most historically important years of their lives.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Mar. 16, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 31 (Biographies, UF Bio-pics)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yee, M.M. Moving image materials, 1988:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Screen biographies"}}, {"@id": "_:na0b03fcf02b94cb8863d35bff9a87702b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFo