munity organizations, often church or civic groups, frequently including a history of the organization and the region, personal recollections or local culinary traditions.", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010025051"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-03-13T13:23:02"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-05T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Community cookbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(titles: Nidkids fundraising cookbook 2001; Artists & art lovers cookbook : a fundraising appeal for the new Christchurch Art Gallery; Best in the West cookbook : a St Leonards Road School PTA fundraising project; The CKFM Bonnie Stern cookbook : a fundraising project in support of the Hospital for Sick Children; Fund raising cook book / Anti-Cancer Council of Victoria; The Toronto celebrity cookbook : a fund-raising project for the Boys & Girls Club of Downtown Toronto; The city of Olathe 150th anniversary community cookbook, 1857-2007; Hesperia Public Library community cookbook; Park Avenue Synagogue community cookbook; Grow, cook, and celebrate : a community recipe book; Prospect School recipe book; Everman Garden Club & community recipe book; Woodbury community recipes)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "OCLC, June 21, 2010", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "St. John Lutheran Church cookbook, 2014.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "FM94.9 WQMX Akron's country station 2002 charity cookbook for Battered Women's Shelter of Summit & Medina Counties, \u00a92002.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grace Lutheran Church Women cookbook, c1983.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "The Auburn cook book / compiled by ladies of the church of the Holy Family, Auburn, Washington, 1916.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cookbooks (Types of cookbooks: Community cookbooks (also known as compiled, regional, charitable, and fund-raising cookbooks) are a unique genre of culinary literature. Community cookbooks focus on home cooking, often documenting regional, ethnic, family, and societal traditions, as well as local history)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Dec. 28, 2017:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "American Legion Auxiliary cook book, 1950?", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "McIntosh Presbyterian Church cookbook, 2013.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(contents include: Church cookbooks : changing foodways on the American prairie / Rubie Watson)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The handbook of food and anthropology, 2016", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b14", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(contents include: \"Tried receipts\" : an overview of America's charitable cookbooks / Janice Bluestein Longone)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Recipes for reading : community cookbooks, stories, histories, \u00a91997", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b15", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: The LaConner cook book : choice and tested receipts/furnished by the ladies of LaConner, Washington; arranged by the Ladies of the Catholic Mite Society, 188-.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b16", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. iv (\"This study examines late Victorian Protestant church community cookbooks as moral and cultural guides written by women for women ... It then examines church community cookbooks as uniquely viable and valuable historical and autobiographical sources through which to better understand Christian domestic practice in Victorian America.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Bailey, E.J. \"Eateth not the bread of idleness\" : church cookbooks and Victorian American domesticity, 2010:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b17", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(compiled by the American Women's Club of Auckland)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The community charity cookbook, 1997", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b18", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Downsview kicks it up a notch! : Government of Canada Workplace Charitable Campaign cookbook, 2003.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b19", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Covenant Moravian Church cookbook, 2014?", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b20", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b21"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fund raising cookbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b21", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fund raising cookbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b23", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b24"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Charity cookbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b24", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Charity cookbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b26", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b27"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fundraising cookbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b27", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fundraising cookbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b29", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b30"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Church cookbooks (Community cookbooks)"}}, {"@id": "_:n198f4ad9261a4de6992834bd61ad6406b30", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormEle