guage": "en", "@value": "Martial arts television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2101227c1e224a9c85cb971382014ba0b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Fictional work designed to showcase the hero's athletic agility and ability to turn his body into a weapon. This skill has been achieved through his dedication to, and personification of, Oriental teachings about physical and mental discipline. Used for Kung fu)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Moving image genre-form guide online, August 9, 2007", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2101227c1e224a9c85cb971382014ba0b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 62 (Martial arts films and programs: use for fictional genre films and programs which consist largely of choreographed fight sequences employing martial arts which originally developed in the Orient)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yee, Martha M. Moving image materials : genre terms, 1988:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2101227c1e224a9c85cb971382014ba0b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2101227c1e224a9c85cb971382014ba0b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kung fu television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2101227c1e224a9c85cb971382014ba0b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kung fu television programs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026389"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026390", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMedical films (Motion pictures)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026390", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b1"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical films (Motion pictures)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026406"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b5"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b6"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b7"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b8"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b11"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Fiction or nonfiction films that feature medical personnel and the practice of medicine.", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007025655"}}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-02T14:00:04"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical films (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Medical: fictional work telling of the milieu of health practitioners, from doctors to nurses, their profession, and their patients. Romances among them are frequent, and the presentation ranges from the most scandalous behavior to idealized portraits of selfless doctors and nurses. The milieu may be portrayed under both emergency as well as day-to-day conditions, with patients struggling to overcome physical and sometimes mental challenges; Medical (Nonfiction): Predominantly nontheatrical work documenting medical operations, procedures, or conditions, or work designed for medical personnel)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Moving image genre-form guide online, December 17, 2007", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 62 (Medical films and programs: use for fictional genre films and programs in which the progagonists are doctors and plot revolves around the saving of life)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yee, M.M. Moving image materials, 1988:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Hospital, 1970.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b8", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b9"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Doctor films (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b9", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Doctor films (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b11", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b12"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hospital films (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n78b2327e0b8f4fbe95a20b6095a8b744b12", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hospital films (Motion pictures)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026390"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026391", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMedical radio programs", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026391", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb1"}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical radio programs"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026506"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb5"}, "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb6"}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb9"}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb12"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Fiction or nonfiction radio programs that feature medical personnel and the practice of medicine.", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008025677"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T10:47:47"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical radio programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(medical drama: Fictional programs in which the protagonist(s) are medical personnel and the plot takes place in a medical setting; UF Doctor dramas, Hospital dramas, Nurse dramas)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Radio genre-form guide online, Oct. 27, 2008", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Doctor radio programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Doctor radio programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb9", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb10"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hospital radio programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb10", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hospital radio programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nurse radio programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c33be3dc0354557a0b43e6ffb308c6eb13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nurse radio programs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026391"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026392", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMedical television programs", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026392", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab1"}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical television programs"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026673"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab5"}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab7"}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab10"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Fiction or nonfiction television programs that feature medical personnel and the practice of medicine.", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007025654"}}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-02T14:00:51"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Medical: fictional work telling of the milieu of health practitioners, from doctors to nurses, their profession, and their patients. Romances among them are frequent, and the presentation ranges from the most scandalous behavior to idealized portraits of selfless doctors and nurses. The milieu may be portrayed under both emergency as well as day-to-day conditions, with patients struggling to overcome physical and sometimes mental challenges; Medical (Nonfiction): Predominantly nontheatrical work documenting medical operations, procedures, or conditions, or work designed for medical personnel)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Moving image genre-form guide online, December 17, 2007", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 62 (Medical films and programs: use for fictional genre films and programs in which the progagonists are doctors and plot revolves around the saving of life)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yee, M.M. Moving image materials, 1988:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hospital television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hospital television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Doctor television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:nf3bb844819234e7d8fe2e70e48bf59eab11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Doctor television programs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026392"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026393", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMelodramas (Motion pictures)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026393", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb1"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Melodramas (Motion pictures)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026250"}, "madsrdf:hasEarlierEstablishedForm": {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb5"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb8"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb10"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb13"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb16"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:useFor": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026422"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008025565"}]}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-28T09:33:07"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Melodramas (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb5", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb6"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Niskavouri films"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb6", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Niskavouri films"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Melodrama: fictional work emphasizing emotional vicissitudes and tragic occurrences, traditionally presented in an overwrought manner. The plot usually concerns victimized or suffering protagonists and a mixture of difficulties among lovers, family, friends, or the community. The story typically encompasses both familial and romantic themes)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Moving image genre-form guide online, April 7, 2008", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 63 (Melodrama: use for fictional genre films which revolve around relatively passive, suffering protagonists, victimized by situations or events related to society, family, and/or sexuality. Emotion, rather than action, is emphasized, and is usually expressed through music, mise en scene, and production design, as well as character portrayal. The narrative is set in contemporary times and is usually resolved by a \"happy ending.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yee, M.M. Moving image materials, 1988:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Melodrama films"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Melodrama films"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Niskavouri films"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Niskavouri films"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Melodramatic films"}}, {"@id": "_:nd7d4938924b64842809698399091d63eb17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Melodramatic films"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026393"}
