ties/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Television programs that comically imitate another work or group of works of a more serious nature. For television programs that use wit, irony, or sarcasm to hold up human vices or foibles to ridicule or scorn see [Satirical television programs.]", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007025345"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-01T09:57:04"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Parody television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(spoof 3. A gentle satirical imitation; a light parody)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Am. herit. dict. of the Eng. lang., c2000", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(spoof 1. a mocking imitation of someone or something, usually light and good-humored; lampoon or parody)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Random House Web. unabr. dict., c1997", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(spoof n. 2: a light, amiable, humorous but usu. telling takeoff (as on human nature, customs, or manners) : parody)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Web. 3", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(spoof noun (Informal) parody, take-off (informal), satire, caricature, mockery, send-up (Brit. informal), travesty, lampoon, burlesque)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Collins thesaurus of the English language, via TheFreeDictionary website, Dec. 8, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"Portlandia,\" the new cable television sendup of the Rose City; Television sendup of girls from Brown; a television sendup of the hero shows of the 80s (Knight Rider, Six Million Dollar Man, A-Team, Street Hawk, etc.); a reality-TV sendup; the BBC television send-up of life in the wartime Home Guard; \"The Colbert Report,\" television send-up of right-wing punditry; a television takeoff on Scrooge; television takeoffs; television take-offs)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Google search, Dec. 8, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "thesaurus (spoof - a composition that imitates or misrepresents somebody's style, usually in a humorous way: parody, pasquinade, put-on, sendup, charade, lampoon, mockery, burlesque, travesty, takeoff)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "TheFreeDictionary website, Dec. 8, 2012:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(parodies: use for films or programs which borrow genre or form conventions, but use them in a mocking or nonsensical manner in order to ridicule or satirize genres, forms and formula, and/or the societies which produce them; UF spoofs)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yee, M. Moving image materials : genre terms, 1988", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Send-up television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Send-up television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television sendups"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television sendups"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television takeoffs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television takeoffs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television parodies"}}, {"@id": "_:n5cace8f36813410883a0affa12c74b39b22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television parodies"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ca