@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-08-03T13:42:12"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Peplum films"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 17 (peplum films) p. 103 (pepla)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "G\u00fcnsberg, M. Italian cinema : gender and genre, 2005:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(peplum: see Ancient world; Fantasy)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Moving image genre-form guide via WWW, July 19, 2007:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(term Peplum most commonly applied to the mass of muscle-man movies that sprung up in the 1960s after the success of Hercules (1958). However, like most euro-cult expressions it has become confused and re-used heavily down the years, most often interchangably with the generic term \"Sword and Sandal\" leading to many American made films being rather incorrectly classified as Pepla; incorporating the traditional muscleman films as well as historical epics and adventure pictures with a classical/ancient setting (from Ancient Egypt through to around 700 AD) but not including more modern-set historical epics and muscleman films or the Biblical epics of which the Italians shot many during the 1960s; The Peplum should also not be confused with the later \"Sword and Scorcery\" genre that arose from the success of Conan the Barbarian (1982) and although there is a lot of overlap, the latter distinctly employed more high fantasy and magical elements)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The Mondo-Esoterica guide to the peplum, via WWW, May 2, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(peplum films: 18,100 hits; cloak-and-sandal films: 2 hits; muscleman films: 419 hits; pepla: 28,500 hits; sex-and-sand epics: 213 hits; Spear-and-sandal epics: 197 hits)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Google, July 14, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Peplum (Sex-and-Sand Epic, S & S Movie); Peplums are minor epics featuring mythological, biblical, and Italian-created strongmen elevated to the category of popular heroes: Hercules, Maciste, Ursus, Samson, Goliath, Taur; has also been referred to as sword-and-sandal epic, sandal-and-spear/s epic, spear-and-sandal epic, cloak-and sandal, gladiator, and muscle/muscleman epic)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "L\u00f3pez, D. Films by genre, \u00a91993", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(summary: When a Roman general is betrayed and his family murdered by an emperor's corrupt son, he comes to Rome as a gladiator to seek revenge)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Gladiator (Motion picture : 2000). Gladiator, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 5 (the peplum; pepla; peplum or sword and sandal films)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Of muscles and men : essays on the sword and sandal film, \u00a92011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Pepla (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Pepla (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Spear-and-sandal epics (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Spear-and-sandal epics (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sex-and-sand epics (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sex-and-sand epics (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Muscleman films"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Muscleman films"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b24", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b25"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sword-and-sandal epics (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b25", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sword-and-sandal epics (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b27", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b28"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Gladiator films"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b28", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Gladiator films"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b30", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b31"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sandal-and-spear epics (Motion pictures)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0be1f29f31064c6fa33daaf4dc8d30d7b31", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sandal-and-spear epics (Motion pictures)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026439"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026440", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPhysical maps", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026440", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b1"}, {"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Physical maps"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under [Topographic maps]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026387"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Maps that represent the surface of the land or floor of the ocean without man-made structures or vegetation. For maps that represent the horizontal and vertical locations of natural and man-made features see [Topographic maps.]", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009025080"}}, {"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-01T09:57:31"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Physical maps"}}, {"@id": "_:n2631cdddd0f349a38fdf38e8d603b1c9b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "map, physical (A map representing the surface of the land or the floor of the oceans. In addition to representing the relief, physical maps show some natural phenomena such as oceanic currents, swamps, sands and deserts. Man-made structures or vegetation are not shown)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Glossary of the mapping sciences, 1994:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026440"}
