"Pornographic television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d9a235967ea441180132223e7e6166fb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(pornography: Work representing persons engaged in explicit, usually unfaked, sexual acts with a primary intent of arousing viewers)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Moving image genre-form guide online, Jan. 7, 2008", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026461"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026462", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPortolan charts", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026462", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b1"}, {"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Portolan charts"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026387"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b5"}, {"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b6"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Early modern charts of the sea and adjacent coastlines that feature distorted coastlines, networks of rhumb lines, and approximate bearings and estimated distances.", "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009025084"}}, {"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T10:51:59"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Portolan charts"}}, {"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "portolan chart (a chart of the sea and adjacent coastlines which is not drawn on a specific map projection and whose outlines are drawn over a network of rhumb lines corresponding to the directions of the winds and which show approximate bearings and estimated distances. Portolan charts date from the 13th to 17th centuries. The term originally described written sailing instructions for sailors, sometimes accompanied by charts. In the late 19th century it was mistakenly applied to the charts themselves, and in particular to the earlier charts of the 13th to 15th centuries)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Glossary of the mapping sciences, 1994:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7524140f8d984e06b18d102a09e063a6b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Charts--Portolan (a class of early coastal charts capable of navigational use which feature a network of interconnected lines (usually termed rhumb lines); place names written inland at right angles to the coast; drawn in ink on one or more skins following established color conventions; with coastlines shown in a general fashion with bays and headlines exaggerated and navigational hazards marked with crosses and dots)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Form/genre for cartographic materials [draft of LC working group], 1996:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026462"}
