3285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety shows (Radio programs)"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(hdg: Variety shows (Radio programs))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, Oct. 31, 2007", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Variety: Programs that feature various kinds of acts, including comedy, skits and/or music. For comedy-variety programs, use two genres: Comedies and Variety. For musical-variety programs, use two or more genres: Variety and the appropriate LCSH music heading)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Radio form/genre terms guide, via WWW, Oct. 31, 2007", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Radio variety shows"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Radio variety shows"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety programs (Radio programs)"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety programs (Radio programs)"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety radio programs"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda73285e0e145559b12fbf4e4989c04b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety radio programs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026719"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026720", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aVariety shows (Television programs)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026720", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb1"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety shows (Television programs)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026425"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb5"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb6"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb7"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb8"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb11"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb14"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007025576"}}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-01-04T11:58:08"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-09T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety shows (Television programs)"}}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety programs (Variety shows almost always featured musical (instrumental, vocal, and dance) performances and comedy sketches, and sometimes acrobatics, animal or magic tricks, and dramatic recitations; variety...emphasized presentational or performative aspects--immediacy, spontaneity, and spectacle--over storyline and character development)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The encyclopedia of television online, via the Museum of Broadcast Communications web site, Nov. 15, 2007:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 101 (Variety: use for works which consist of a number of different kinds of acts, including such things as stand-up comedieans, comic skits, songs, dance numbers, etc.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yee, M.M. Moving image materials, 1988:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Variety: work that is generally hosted and consists of a number of different acts, sketches, and/or dance and musical performances, combined in a non-narrative manner. Although predominantly for television, some theatrical film variety work has also been produced)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Moving image genre-form guide online, November 15, 2007", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb8", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb9"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb9", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb11", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb12"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety programs (Television programs)"}}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb12", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety programs (Television programs)"}}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television variety shows"}}, {"@id": "_:n070ed46c3ca04c15a36205888793463fb15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Television variety shows"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026720"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026721", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aVector data", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2011026721", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b1"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Vector data"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026297"}, "madsrdf:hasReciprocalAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026520"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b5"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b6"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b7"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b8"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:useFor": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010025024"}}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-09T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2011-05-19T07:41:13"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Vector data"}}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "vector (1. A physical quantity having both length and direction. Velocity, acceleration and force are the most common instances of vectors in physics.  2. A number in the complex plane; a complex number. 3.  A matrix having N rows and 1 column or 1 row and N columns; N is an integer.  4.  A mathematical entity representable as a directed line-segment)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Glossary of the mapping sciences, 1994:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "glossary (vector data: A data structure used to represent linear geographic features. Features are made of ordered lists of x, y or x, y, z coordinates and are represented by points, lines, or polygons; points connect to become lines, and lines connect to become polygons. Attributes are associated with each feature. See also Raster data.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cartographic materials, 2002, 2005 update via Cataloger's Desktop March 26, 2010:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Maps--Digital--Vector: Digital maps stored as line (or point-arc-point) data)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Form/genre for cartographic materials [draft of LC working group], 1996:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b8", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b9"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Vector maps"}}, {"@id": "_:ncdde1eea51754b0fb187c374371c7347b9", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Vector maps"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026721"}
