n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b33"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b36"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b39"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Nonfiction that presents alternative outcomes of historical events and subsequent changes in history. For works in which the plot or setting assumes an alternative outcome of an historical event see terms for Alternative histories qualified by form, e.g., [Alternative histories (Fiction).]"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2020-02-18T14:24:27"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Counterfactual histories"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "If it had happened otherwise : lapses into imaginary history, 1932.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(book genre called alternative history, or speculative history, or counterfactual history or hypothetical history; nonfiction historical fiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Arnold, M. The 'what ifs' that fascinate, via New York times, Dec. 21, 2000, viewed online Aug. 5, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Unmaking the West : \"what-if?\" scenarios that rewrite world history, c2006.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Swedin, E.G. When angels wept : a what-if history of the Cuban Missile Crisis, c2010.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Virtual history : alternatives and counterfactuals, 1999.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Imaginary histories. Here are entered speculative works of history that present alternative outcomes of historical events and subsequent changes in history. Collections of fiction in which the plot or setting assumes an alternative outcome of an historical event are entered under Alternative histories (Fiction). UF Alternate histories (History); Alternative histories (History); History, Imaginary)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Greenfield, J. Then everything changed : stunning alternate histories of American politics : JFK, RFK, Carter, Ford, Reagan, c2011.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Hitler triumphant! : alternate histories of World War II, 2011.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "abstract (A counterfactual is speculating on the consequences if particular events had not happened as they did. For example, suppose the British had won the American Revolutionary War. What would have been the British policy in North America? As law teachers, lawyers, and perhaps policy makers, counterfactual history has much value for us. Its value, however, clearly depends upon the care we take in choosing a plausible counterfactual assertion, the degree of its breadth or, alternatively, its limited nature, and how we make use of the counterfactual)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Landever, A.R. Does counterfactual history have any lessons for law teachers and lawyers? Does it have any value for you, in particular, in your area of research or teaching?, 2003, via EngagedScholarship@CSU website, Aug. 5, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b14", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Counterfactual history, also sometimes referred to as virtual history, is a form of historiography that attempts to answer \"what if\" questions known as counterfactuals. Black and MacRaild provide this definition: \"It is, at the very root, the idea of conjecturing on what did not happen, or what might have happened, in order to understand what did happen. The method seeks to explore history and historical incidents by means of extrapolating a timeline in which certain key historical events did not happen or had an outcome which was different from that which did in fact occur. It has produced a book genre which is variously called alternative history, speculative history, counterfactual history, or hypothetical history)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Aug. 5, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b15", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "preface (counterfactuals; the genre; 'alternate' histories; counterfactual history)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Evans, R.J. Altered pasts : counterfactuals in history, 2013:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b16", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Venning, T. An alternative history of Britain, 2014.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b17", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "cover (imaginary history from twelve leading historians)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "What might have been, 2004:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b18", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "home page (\"The Counterfactual History Review surveys the world of historical speculation, collecting and commenting upon examples of counterfactual reasoning that have appeared in recent books, journal articles, reviews, and online texts. It features occasional reviews of alternate history novels and films, as well as links to news stories that reflect the impact of speculative historical thinking on popular culture.\"; alternate histories of Nazism; Jewish alternate histories)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The counterfactual history review, via WWW, Aug. 5, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b19", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "If the Allies had fallen : sixty alternate scenarios of World War II, c2010.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b20", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Becket, F. The prime ministers who never were : a collection of counterfactuals, 2012.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hypothetical histories"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hypothetical histories"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b24", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b25"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Counterfactuals"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b25", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Counterfactuals"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b27", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b28"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Speculative histories"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b28", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Speculative histories"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b30", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b31"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alternative histories (Nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b31", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alternative histories (Nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b33", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b34"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Histories, Alternative (Nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b34", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Histories, Alternative (Nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b36", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b37"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Imaginary histories"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b37", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Imaginary histories"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b39", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b40"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alternate histories (Nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n7205319fad6a4d63b621f855d307a256b40", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alternate histories (Nonfiction)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026072"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026073", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCourse materials", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026073", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b1"}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Course materials"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026093"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026114"}], "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026069"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b5"}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b6"}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b7"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Handouts and other ephemeral materials used in coursework."}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T16:23:12"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Course materials"}}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "course material (Course materials consist of lecture notes, supplementary reading or exercises, and links to other sites or software.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Evolution at NYU website, Aug. 6, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "ERIC thesaurus, via WWW, Aug. 6, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}, {"@id": "_:n2c69848df8654d04b564e90bca49d651b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(online materials to cover individual topics or learning objectives. Open Course Materials are part of a larger category of Open Educational Resources (OER) that includes whole courses, open textbooks, as well as small instructional modules that make up the Open Course Materials.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Thousands of free online course materials are available and easy to find, via California State University Affordable Learning Solutions website, Aug. 6, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026073"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026074", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCreative nonfiction", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026074", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab1"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Creative nonfiction"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026049"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026072"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026085"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026094"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026142"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026200"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026202"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026203"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026454"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2017026121"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2023026010"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab5"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab6"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab7"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab8"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab9"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab10"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab11"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab12"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab13"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab14"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab17"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab20"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab23"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab26"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab29"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab32"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab35"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab38"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab41"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab44"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab47"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab50"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab53"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab56"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Prose works that use literary styles and techniques to present factually accurate narratives in a compelling manner."}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T16:20:30"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Creative nonfiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(nonfictional prose: any literary work that is based mainly on fact, even though it may contain fictional elements; examples are the essay and biography; the term nonfictional prose literature here designates writing intended to instruct (but does not include highly scientific and erudite writings in which no aesthetic concern is evinced), to persuade, to convert, or to convey experience or reality through \"factual\" or spiritual revelation; one feature common to most authors of nonfictional prose is the marked degree of the author's presence in all they write; the basic modes of writing--the descriptive, the narrative, the expository, and the argumentative--are found in both nonfictional literature and in fiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Britannica online academic edition, Nov. 14, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Prose literature. BT Literature)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 1 (nonfiction genres: true adventure; travel; true crime; environmental writing)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cords, S.S. The real story : a guide to nonfiction reading interests, 2006:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. v (Fourth Genre: Explorations in Nonfiction is a new literary journal devoted solely to works of contemporary nonfiction (the \"fourth genre\"), extending from the personal essay--including nature, environmental, and travel writing--to memoir, literary journalism, and personal cultural criticism)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Fourth genre, spring 1999:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Creative nonfiction. Here are entered works that use literary styles and techniques to present factually accurate narratives in a compelling, vivid manner. UF Fourth genre (Creative nonfiction); Literary nonfiction; Narrative nonfiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(nonfiction literature: this subject area containsstudy guides on literature in nonfiction, a genre in which accounts or representations of subjects are presented as fact; it is generally assumed that the authors of such accounts believe them to be true at the time of their composition)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikibooks, Nov. 15, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(tale: a fictitious or true narrative or story, especially one that is imaginatively recounted.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxford dictionaries website, Apr. 11, 2013", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(in titles: creative nonfiction; creative non-fiction; non-fictional prose; nonfictional prose; nonfiction prose; non-fiction prose; nonfiction literature; non-fiction literature; non-fictional literature; literary nonfiction; literary non-fiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "OCLC, Aug. 12, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "pp. ix-x (when I say \"nonfiction\" in this book, I mean what we usually refer to as \"creative nonfiction\" or \"literary nonfiction.\" Those terms are slippery enough in their own rights that I'll mostly avoid them. Here, nonfiction, the fourth genre, refers to such forms of writing as the personal or familiar or reflective essay, the memoir in short or long forms, personal narrative reportage of travel and place and exploration and investigation; nonfiction can be identified by these common elements: personal presence, self-discovery and self-motivation, flexibility of form, veracity, and literary approaches) pp. 3-4 (the term \"creative nonfiction\" is too oppositional, implying a need to distinguish it from \"non-creative nonfiction\"; Nonfiction, n. : 1. the written expression of, reflection upon, and/or interpretation of observed, perceived, or recollected experience; 2. a genre of literature made up of such writing, which includes such subgenres as the personal essay, the memoir, narrative reportage, and expressive critical writing and whose borders with other reality-based genres and forms (such as journalism, criticism, history, etc.) are fluid and malleable; 3. the expressive, transactional, and poetic prose texts generated by students in college composition courses; 4. (obsolete) not fiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Root, R. The nonfictionist's guide : on reading and writing creative nonfiction, 2008:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fictional prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fictional prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab17", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab18"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfiction prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab18", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfiction prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab20", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab21"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Literary non-fiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab21", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Literary non-fiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab23", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab24"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Prose literature (Creative nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab24", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Prose literature (Creative nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab26", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab27"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Tales (Creative nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab27", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Tales (Creative nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab29", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab30"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Literary nonfiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab30", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Literary nonfiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab32", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab33"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fiction literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab33", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fiction literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab35", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab36"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fictional literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab36", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fictional literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab38", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab39"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfiction literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab39", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfiction literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab41", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab42"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fourth genre (Creative nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab42", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fourth genre (Creative nonfiction)"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab44", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab45"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfictional literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab45", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfictional literature"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab47", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab48"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fiction prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab48", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Non-fiction prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab50", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab51"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfictional prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab51", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Nonfictional prose"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab53", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab54"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Creative non-fiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab54", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Creative non-fiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab56", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab57"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Narrative nonfiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n85e15ad231b546abb656de3eb452ceaab57", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Narrative nonfiction"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026074"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026075", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCrossword puzzles", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026075", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb1"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Crossword puzzles"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2023026014"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb5"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb6"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb7"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb8"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb10"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2023-07-07T14:52:27"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Crossword puzzles"}}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 37 (crossword (puzzle): to be filled in from clues provided)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "G\u00f6rlach, M. An alphabetical list of English text types, in Text types and the history of English, c2004:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(crossword (also crossword puzzle): A puzzle consisting of a grid of squares and blanks into which words crossing vertically and horizontally are written according to clues.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxford dictionaries website, July 26, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Crossword. A crossword is a word puzzle that normally takes the form of a square or a rectangular grid of white and black shaded squares. The goal is to fill the white squares with letters, forming words or phrases, by solving clues which lead to the answers. In languages that are written left-to-right, the answer words and phrases are placed in the grid from left to right and from top to bottom. The shaded squares are used to separate the words or phrases.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, July 26, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(crossword: a puzzle in which words are filled into a pattern of numbered squares in answer to correspondingly numbered clues and in such a way that the words read across and down)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Merriam-Webster online, July 26, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(crossword puzzle: a puzzle in which words corresponding to numbered clues or definitions are supplied and fitted into correspondingly numbered sets of squares, one letter per square, the words being arranged horizontally or vertically so that most letters form part of two words.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Dictionary.com, July 26, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Crosswords"}}, {"@id": "_:n8d08f16606694939b7504304d827901fb11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Crosswords"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026075"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026076", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCruise books", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026076", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b1"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cruise books"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026064"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026111"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b5"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b6"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b7"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b8"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b10"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Pictorial publications that document a voyage of a particular ship and are distributed to the ship's crew."}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T16:20:58"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cruise books"}}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "USS San Antonio maiden deployment, 2008-2009 cruise book, 2009?", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "USS O'Brien DD-975, 1997-1998 cruisebook, 1998?", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cruise books. Use for pictorial publications, usually amateur in nature, documenting a voyage of a particular ship and distributed to the ship's crew. BT Illustrated works; Keepsakes)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Genre terms : a thesaurus for use in rare book and special collections cataloging, via WWW, July 26 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cruise book of the U.S.S. Canberra (CAG-2) Presidential Cruise, 1957, 1957.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Rendezvous with Antarctica, 1958-59 : U.S.S. Staten Island (AGB-5), Operation Deepfreeze IV cruisebook, 1959?", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cruisebooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n2295fb10d1a44103853a3eaf63ca0211b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cruisebooks"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026076"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026077", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCryptograms", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026077", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb1"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cryptograms"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026158"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb5"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb6"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb7"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb8"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb9"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Puzzles that consist of a short encrypted text."}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T16:21:12"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cryptograms"}}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cryptograms. BT Puzzles)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 37 (cryptogram/-graph: coded message)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "G\u00f6rlach, M. An alphabetical list of English text types, in Text types and the history of English, c2004:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(A cryptogram is a type of puzzle that consists of a short piece of encrypted text. Generally the cipher used to encrypt the text is simple enough that cryptogram can be solved by hand. Frequently used are substitution ciphers where each letter is replaced by a different letter or number. To solve the puzzle, one must recover the original lettering. Though once used in more serious applications, they are now mainly printed for entertainment in newspapers and magazines.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, July 26, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(cryptogram 1. A text written in code. 2. A symbol or figure with secret or occult significance.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxford dictionaries website, July 26, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb9", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb10"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cryptographs"}}, {"@id": "_:n99c2381a833948069d8f21060ab5b22cb10", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cryptographs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026077"}
