 "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Finding Aid: A descriptive tool providing access to a resource.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "RDA glossary, viewed July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n94ae0cbd81cf464a8ae1c9ab42a9758eb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(finding tool: A general term for a resource designed to be used in a library to locate sources of information, usually in a search by author, title, subject, or keywords. The category includes catalogs, bibliographies, indexes, abstracting services, bibliographic databases, etc. The corresponding term in archives is finding aid.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary for library and information science, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n94ae0cbd81cf464a8ae1c9ab42a9758eb7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n94ae0cbd81cf464a8ae1c9ab42a9758eb8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Archival finding aids"}}, {"@id": "_:n94ae0cbd81cf464a8ae1c9ab42a9758eb8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Archival finding aids"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026103"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026104", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aFlag books", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026104", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab1"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flag books"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026197"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab5"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab6"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab7"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab8"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab9"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab10"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab11"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Books that consist of rows of tabs of paper attached to an accordion-folded spine, allowing for the layering of complementary or contrasting images and narratives."}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T16:25:12"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flag books"}}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "t.p. (Flag Books are fancy and fun because... They move--watch those flags fly! When they stand up they make great displays for your art. They can be a group project with each person contributing a flag.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Flag books, via Booklyn Artists Alliance website, Feb. 23, 2012:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Flag books (Toy and movable books). UF Flagbooks (Toy and movable books). BT Toy and movable books. Here are entered works on books that consist of rows of flags attached to an accordion-folded spine, allowing for the layering of complementary or contrasting images and narratives.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Flagbooks use an accordion spine to hold the pages, which look like little flags. These books shine when in motion and made great sound effects!)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Flagbook in motion, via YouTube website, Feb. 23, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Create a unique 'flag' book which allows you to experiment with a selection of mini pages or 'flags'. As the book is opened, the pages move in opposite directions. These can be used to create pockets for keepsakes, artists trading cards or postcard sized works of art. From crafting the cover and mastering the 'mechanics' of the construction, to designing and filling the inside pages, this is a unique and unusual way to collect keepsakes or present your art.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Making a flagbook, via polkadotcreative.com website, Feb. 23, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "galleries > 100th anniversary exhibition > retrospective exhibition > Kyle (the form that has become known as the \"Flag Book.\" It is the single most influential structure in the world of contemporary bookmaking. This method of construction, employing tipped on page fragments on alternating sides of a concertina structure, has been adopted by artists worldwide for the creation of unique and multiple bookworks)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Guild of Book Workers home page, Feb. 23, 2012:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flagbook bind-o-rama (Originally developed by Hedi Kyle; the foundation of the deceptively simple Flag Book structure is an accordion folded spine. Rows of flags attached to opposing sides of each of the spine's \"mountain\" folds allow the artist to fragment and layer a number of complementary or contrasting images and narratives)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Book Arts Web, Feb. 23, 2012:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab11", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab12"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flagbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n58635d6c2147406197c215242464838ab12", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flagbooks"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026104"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026105", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aFlip books", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026105", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb1"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flip books"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026197"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb5"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb7"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb10"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb13"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb16"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Books that consist of a series of illustrations bound together in a sequence so that they create an illusion of animation when flipped rapidly."}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T16:25:23"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flip books"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Flip books. Use for books containing a series of images bound together in sequence so that an illusion of movement can be imparted by flipping them rapidly. UF Books, flip; Corner-flip movies; Flipbooks. BT Illustrated works)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Genre terms : a thesaurus for use in rare book and special collections cataloging, via WWW, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(flicker book: A type of toy book published during the 19th century containing a sequence of closely related cartoon-style illustrations designed to give the impression of animation when the pages are fanned from cover to cover, similar to the illusion of movement created by the rapid projection of frames in a motion picture. Synonymous with flip book; flip book See: flicker book)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary for library and information science, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flicker books"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flicker books"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Corner-flip movies"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Corner-flip movies"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flipbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Flipbooks"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Movies, Corner-flip"}}, {"@id": "_:n390699a4e51f4b339383c8ecaaefe65fb17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Movies, Corner-flip"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026105"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026106", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aGenealogical tables", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026106", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb1"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Genealogical tables"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under [Family histories]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026186"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb5"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb6"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb7"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb8"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb9"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb10"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb11"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb12"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb13"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb14"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb17"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb20"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb23"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Lineages of people or purebred animals in tabular or diagrammatic form. For narrative studies of families and the tracing of their lineages and histories see [Family histories.]"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2020-02-18T14:24:27"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Genealogical tables"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Biographical sketch and genealogical tree of the Lalkaka family, 1690 to 30th June 1910, 1910?", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Genealogies. UF Family trees. BT Historical works. Use for family trees and other listings of family members. For narrative histories, use \"Family histories.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Genre terms : a thesaurus for use in rare book and special collections cataloging, via WWW, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(pedigree. A genealogical table. The first collections of pedigrees were made in the 15th century. Pedigrees were a matter of aristocratic pride and of practical necessity for legal purposes. In the reigns of Elizabeth I, James I, and Charles I they were often displayed as colourful works of art.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The Oxford companion to local and family history, 1996", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(genealogical table: A diagram, usually in the form of an inverted tree, with branches showing the lineage of a person or group of persons who share a common ancestor, sometimes printed on the endpapers of biographical or historical works, particularly those concerning the reigns of sovereigns or the lives of titled nobility; family tree: A diagram, chart, or other graphic representation of the genealogy of a family, often a branched figure showing the descendants of a given pair of progenitors. The category includes decorative or pictorial charts containing blank spaces for the insertion of names and/or portraits.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary for library and information science, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(genealogical tables. UF family trees. Documents representing the lineage of a person or persons in tabular or diagrammatic form.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Art & architecture thesaurus online, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(pedigree 1. an ancestral line; line of descent; lineage; ancestry. 2. a genealogical table, chart, list, or record, especially of a purebred animal. 3. distinguished, excellent, or pure ancestry. 4. derivation, origin, or history)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Dictionary.com, Sept. 9, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(pedigree 1. The record of descent of an animal, showing it to be purebred. 2. The recorded ancestry, especially upper-class ancestry, of a person or family. 2.1 The background or history of a person or thing, especially as conferring distinction or quality. 2.2 A genealogical table.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxford dictionaries website, Sept. 9, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Genealogical Table: An illustrative content consisting of a table or diagram representing the lineage of a person or family.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "RDA glossary, viewed July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(genealogical table. A representation of the lineage of a person or persons in tabular or diagrammatical form.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harrod, L.M. The librarians' glossary of terms used in librarianship and the book crafts and reference book, 1971", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Family trees"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Family trees"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb17", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb18"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Genealogical trees"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb18", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Genealogical trees"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb20", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb21"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Genealogies (Tables)"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb21", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Genealogies (Tables)"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb23", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb24"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Pedigrees (Genealogical tables)"}}, {"@id": "_:n5ce8025c420d4861a197b11284452a6eb24", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Pedigrees (Genealogical tables)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026106"}
