c"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n57b5150eec3649d38558ff662fa390a7b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Lift-the-flap books"}}, {"@id": "_:n57b5150eec3649d38558ff662fa390a7b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Lift-the-flap books. BT Toy and movable books)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n57b5150eec3649d38558ff662fa390a7b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Tyrrell, M. Let's count bugs : a slide-and-peek book, c1998.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n57b5150eec3649d38558ff662fa390a7b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Flaps: One or more illustrated papers glued at one point. Lifting a flap exposes the illustration directly beneath it (see Lift-the-flap); Lift-the-flap: A single piece of paper attached to the base page at a single point which covers an illustration, text, or a movable illustration. 'Lifting the flap' exposes the base page's illustration, text, or movable.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Glossary of pop-up terms, via WWW, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n57b5150eec3649d38558ff662fa390a7b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Lift-the flaps)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Understanding children's book genres, via WWW, July 30, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n57b5150eec3649d38558ff662fa390a7b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Campbell, R. Dear zoo : a lift-the-flap book, 2007.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n57b5150eec3649d38558ff662fa390a7b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Lift-the-flap books; have cardboard flaps that children can open and close throughout the story; they make books more hands-on and i