{"@language": "en", "@value": "(palindrome: A word, phrase, number, or other sequence of units that reads the same in either direction, for examples, the word \"radar\" or the sentence \"Too far, Edna, we wander afoot.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary of library and information science, July 26, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2961b93af9c5439caa05d7ed3f83fef1b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 60 (palindrome: phrase that reads the same backwards as forewards)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "G\u00f6rlach, M. An alphabetical list of English text types, in Text types and the history of English, c2004:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2961b93af9c5439caa05d7ed3f83fef1b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Palindromes. BT Literary recreations; Puzzles; Word games)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026137"}
