ints; brought to the New World at least as early as 1716 by the Franciscans)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed June 5, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026621"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026622", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aAlal\u00e1s", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026622", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab1"}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alal\u00e1s"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026811"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab5"}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab6"}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab7"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:49"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alal\u00e1s"}}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 99531579: Groba, R. An\u00e1lisis de 252 alal\u00e1s, 1998.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(alal\u00e1: genre of Galician (Spanish) song, characterized by the refrain sung at the end of each verse to the vocables \"ay-la-la\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1790fa0cf8304eafa90fa1e0b4f2565ab7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(alal\u00e1: Galician folk song with \"la-la\" type refrains)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "White, D. Dict. of pop. mus. styles of the world, c1998", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026622"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026623", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $a\u0100l\u0101pa", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026623", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b1"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101pa"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026693"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027180"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b5"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b6"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b7"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b8"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b9"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b10"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b11"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b12"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b13"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b16"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b19"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Unmetered and improvised prelude to the raga in Carnatic music."}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T17:52:32"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101pa"}}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\u0101l\u0101pana, \u0101l\u0101pa, \u0101l\u0101p)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "MGG, 2nd ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Alapa (Sanskrit: 'conversation'; Hindi alap; Urdu alap; Tamil alapanam): in South Asian music, an unmetred introduction to the performance of a metrical composition, comprising an exposition of the mode or raga of the composition; normally improvised according to traditional principles, and is variable in length from a few minutes to an hour or more)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove, 2nd ed. WWW site, Jan. 4, 2001", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "v. 5, p. 975 (\u0101l\u0101p: nonmetric exposition of a raga; introductory section of a raga performance; improvisation within a Hindustani composition)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Garland encyc. of world music:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under India (\u0101l\u0101p (Hindustani music); \u0101l\u0101pana (Carnatic music))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 94907423: P\u0101lacantrar\u0101ju, Es. 100 ir\u0101ka\u1e45ka\u1e37ukk\u0101n\u0332a e\u1e37iya ir\u0101ka \u0101l\u0101pan\u0332ai, 1993.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 172 (the main branch of Indian improvisation, the exposition of a distinctive tonal pattern (r\u0101ga), is called r\u0101ga \u0101l\u0101pana or \u0101l\u0101pana (=\u0101l\u0101p in Hindust\u0101n\u012b music); characterized by the absence of a definable and recurring rhythmic pattern or metre (t\u0101la))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Pesch, L. Ill. companion to South Indian classical music, 1999:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\u0101l\u0101pa: free-lance composition, obviously extempore, to delineate a r\u0101ga by gradual exposition and at the earlier stage free from rhythmic bounds)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "R\u00f4ya Caudhur\u012b, V. Dict. of Hindustani classical music, 2000", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\u0101l\u0101p, \u0101l\u0101pa(na): unmetered and unpulsed, improvised prelude or vocalise in Indian music)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Harvard dict. music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101pana"}}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101pana"}}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101p"}}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101p"}}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b19", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b20"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101panam"}}, {"@id": "_:n95cf198dfc4c4aea91855b15aa393497b20", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "\u0100l\u0101panam"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026623"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026624", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aAleatory music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026624", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b1"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aleatory music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026639"}, "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026975"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b5"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b6"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b7"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b8"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b9"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b10"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b11"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b12"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b13"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b14"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b17"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b20"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Musical compositions created by chance methods or that may be performed in random or indeterminate style."}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T17:52:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aleatory music"}}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatoric, Aleatory; in 1961 quotation: indeterminate, or aleatoric music)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "OED", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatorism: practice of employing an element of chance in the performance of a piece of music; interest in the genre faded somewhat after the 1960s. Indeterminacy: concept introduced by Cage in preference to the term \"aleatorism\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Brewer's twentieth-cent. music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatory music; x-ref from Chance music)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "RILM abstracts", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatory: adj. used of music in which the composer deliberately makes room for chance occurrences or choices by performers; normally reserved for 20th-cent. music beginning with Ives. Indeterminacy: term introduced by Cage and preferred by him to aleatory composition. Chance operations: term used by Cage for compositional methods dependent largely on chance)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Thames and Hudson encyc. of 20th-cent. music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatory: indeterminate. Indeterminate music: music over which the composer has to some degree relinquished control, perhaps by leaving some aspects to chance or to the performer's decision. Chance operations: term introduced by John Cage for techniques which open the compositional process to chance)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Ox. companion to music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatory music: chance music, either in the compositional process or the performer's realization. Chance operations: the practice, highly developed by Cage, of composing music via chance means, resulting in works devoid of compositional taste or intentions. Indeterminacy: with ref. to composition, denotes a conventional score produced by chance; with ref. to performance, a score which leaves much to be determined by performers)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Baker's dict of music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatory music; the term \"chance music\" is preferred by many composers)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Harvard dict. of music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatory music: synonym for indeterminacy. Indeterminacy: much the same as aleatory, but specifically the principle by which a decision of the performer of a composition replaces a decision of the composer. Chance: see Aleatory)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Ox. dict. of music, 2nd ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Aleatory: term applied to music whose composition and/or performance is, to a greater or lesser extent, undetermined by the composer; \"aleatoric\" represents an etymological distortion; x-refs. from Chance, Indeterminacy."}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Indeterminate music (Aleatory music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Indeterminate music (Aleatory music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b17", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b18"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aleatoric music"}}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b18", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aleatoric music"}}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b20", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b21"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Chance music"}}, {"@id": "_:n49b07c7b7afa4930baac491d41595438b21", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Chance music"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026624"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026625", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aAleke", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026625", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b1"}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aleke"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026809"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b5"}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b6"}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b7"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:49"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Aleke"}}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "v. 2, p. 509 (Surinam; aleke; as a more recent contrast to kawina and kaseko, aleke is heavily percussive, featuring Djuka drums in spirit and aleke drums in actuality; in addition, aleke is a vocal music with communication in mind; its lyrics often deal with decidedly modern themes, from AIDS and poverty to the pros and cons of condoms)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Garland encyclopedia of world music, 1998:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "French Guiana (Dances performed by young people for their own amusement (aleke)) Suriname (A recently invented dance and drumming genre, aleke, merges older Ndyuka styles with elements from Creole genres such as kawina and kaseko, serving as an important medium of self-expression for the young)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 8, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n40f233357cf54134bf912b2463e29158b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "label (Dedi\u00e9 \u00e0 tous les groupes aleke) container (aleke) program booklet (Traditional dance music of the Djuka, Paramacca, and Aluku peoples of Surinam and French Guiana. Aleke is essentially a rhythmic pattern played on percussion instruments accompanying both solo and choral singing. The Saramacca people have equivalent patterns called kawina and kase ko. This music is not directly connected to African music or religious practices [even though these peoples are descended from African slaves.])"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 96-705456: Sapatia on the move, ca. 1994:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026625"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026626", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aAll Saints' Day music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026626", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb1"}, {"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "All Saints' Day music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026795"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027062"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Music traditionally associated with All Saints' Day."}, {"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T17:53:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "All Saints' Day music"}}, {"@id": "_:n9683eec29a4d4ebd9ff3e7ffc5ad3cbeb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(All Saints' Day; a solemnity celebrated on 1 November by the Catholic Church and several Protestant denominations, and on the first Sunday after Pentecost in Eastern Catholicism and Eastern Orthodoxy, in honour of all the saints, known and unknown; in English-speaking countries, the festival is traditionally celebrated with the hymn For all the saints by Walsham How; another hymn sung on this day is I sing of the saints of God)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, viewed August 8, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026626"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026627", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aAlleluias (Chants)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026627", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb1"}, {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alleluias (Chants)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027020"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb5"}, "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb6"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:49"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Alleluias (Chants)"}}, {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Chant of the Mass in the Western Church and of the Divine Liturgy in the Eastern Church. The alleluia of the Mass is a Proper chant sung during the Fore-Mass after the gradual ... except on liturgical occasions associated with penitence and fasting (most notably during Lent), and on ones associated with sorrow (such as the Requiem Mass), when it may be replaced by the Tract. During Paschal Time, beginning with Low Sunday, the gradual is omitted and two alleluias are sung. The alleluia is performed in a responsorial manner: first the word 'alleluia' is sung, concluding with an extended melismatic flourish - the Jubilus; then a verse (rarely, two or three verses) is chanted in a moderately elaborate setting; and finally the alleluia is repeated. Throughout much of the Middle Ages a cantor intoned the alleluia without its jubilus and the chorus answered with the entire alleluia; one or two cantors sang the verse and the chorus entered for the final word or two (usually concluding with a melisma echoing that of the jubilus); the chorus, finally, repeated the alleluia. Early sources fail to indicate such involvement by the chorus, but it might well be that the chorus performed at least the final repetition of the alleluia.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed May 28, 2014 :", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Allelujas (Chants)"}}, {"@id": "_:nc4479e1dc03e4727a0c6a48dac9b245cb7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Allelujas (Chants)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026627"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026628", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aAllemandes (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026628", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b1"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Allemandes (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b5"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b7"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b10"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b13"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b16"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:49"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Allemandes (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Allemande; allemand; almain; alman; almond; one of the most popular of Baroque instrumental dances and a standard movement, along with the courante, sarabande and gigue, of the suite; originated some time in the early or mid-16th century)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 8, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Allemande. 1. A Renaissance and Baroque dance that was cultivated as an independent instrumental piece ca. 1580-1750... The allemande originated in the early or mid-16th century as a \"German dance\"...; 2. a dance in triple meter originating in the the mid-18th century... applied loosely to a number of waltzlike dance through the 19th century as an equivalent of \"German dance\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Allemands (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Allemands (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Almans (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Almans (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Almonds (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Almonds (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Almains (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nd79ac4ca795a4cca8e06329bddecc0a5b17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Almains (Music)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026628"}
