ope from the late 16th century to the mid-18th, often as a movement of a suite.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 9, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026741"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026742", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCourt dances (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026742", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb1"}, {"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Court dances (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026656"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:52"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Court dances (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n4cce21620bcd4cf5a98ba0cb98c100abb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Basse danse (the principal court dance during the late middle Ages and Renaissance); under Pavan (a court dance of the 16th and early 17th centuries)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove dict. of mus. WWW site, Feb. 23, 2011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026742"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026743", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCover versions", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026743", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b1"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cover versions"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026594"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b5"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b6"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b7"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b8"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b9"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b10"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b11"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b12"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b13"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b14"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b17"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b20"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b23"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b26"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Cover versions that are explicitly identified as such."}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-14T10:01:27"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cover versions"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover versions: Performances/recordings by musicians not responsible for the original recording; in body of article: covers, cover songs)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Shuker, R. Key concepts in popular music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover: n., 14: music, new recording of well-known song: a recording by a performer of a song that was first sung or popularized by another performer. Also called Cover version)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Encarta world English dict. WWW site, Jan. 17, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover: n.(1), I.f. In full, cover version: A recording of a song, etc., which has already been recorded by someone else)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "OED WWW site, Jan. 17, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover version: A recording of a song that was previously recorded or made popular by another; also called cover song. Cover: n., 11. Music: A cover version)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "American heritage dict., 4th ed., via Bartleby.com, Jan. 17, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 2002487084: Reijt, V. De Nederlandstalige cover top-100 van Vic van de Reijt, 2001.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover (cover version, cover record): A term used in the popular music industry usually for a recording of a particular song by performers other than those responsible for the original recorded version; it may also be applied to a re-recording of a song by the original performers (generally using pseudonyms) for a rival record company)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove, 2nd ed. WWW site, Jan. 17, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover version: In popular music, a recording that remakes an earlier, sometimes very successful, recording. The aim of such a recording, which may or may not directly acknowledge the original, is to reach a wider commercial market, often by adapting the original to the tastes of a new or somewhat different audience (e.g., a rock \"cover\" of a rhythm-and-blues recording))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Harvard dict. mus.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover: To record a song (or even an entire album) that has already been recorded by someone else. The history of jazz, rock, and pop would not be complete without the long list of covers that have actually proved better and often more commercially successful than the originals)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Pickering, D. Cassell companion to 20th-century music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cover version: A recording of a popular song by a performer or performers other than those responsible for the original version; it can be a re-creation of the original or a radical reworking)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxf. comp. mus., 2002", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cover records"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cover records"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b17", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b18"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cover songs"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b18", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cover songs"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b20", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b21"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Records, Cover"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b21", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Records, Cover"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b23", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b24"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Songs, Cover"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b24", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Songs, Cover"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b26", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b27"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Covers (Cover versions)"}}, {"@id": "_:n91b3c7ee7b5446a0b9a4642b97191e64b27", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Covers (Cover versions)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026743"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026744", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCowboy songs", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026744", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b1"}, {"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cowboy songs"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027103"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b5"}, {"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b6"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Music that describes cowboys and the cowboy life."}, {"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2017-04-14T11:40:05"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cowboy songs"}}, {"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cowboy song; a type of song describing cowboys and their life; began to appear in the late 19th century; generally written in ballad style, but are melodically and structurally indebted to traditional popular, folk, and religious songs)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 29, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n846c540a6e6740a5b7485bd5e231c349b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cowboy songs)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "AFS Ethnographic thesaurus", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026744"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026745", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCowpunk music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026745", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb1"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cowpunk music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026739"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027025"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb5"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb6"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb7"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb8"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb9"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb10"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb11"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb12"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb13"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb16"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:52"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cowpunk music"}}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(cowpunk: a musical style combining country-and-western with punk rock; by extension, a performer of this, the culture associated with it)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Dictionary.com, Sept. 13, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cowpunk. A precursor to the alternative country-rock of the decade to follow, Cowpunk was a 1980s phenomenon incorporating the mood and texture of traditional country music with the energy and attitude of punk; listed as a subgenre of Alternative/Indie Rock)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Allmusic.com, Sept. 13, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(cowpunk: a type of popular music combining elements of country and western with those of punk rock.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxford dictionaries online, Sept. 13, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cowpunk (Cowpunk or Country punk is a subgenre of punk rock that began in the UK and California in the late 1970s and early 1980s. It combines punk rock or New Wave with country music, folk music, and blues in sound, subject matter, attitude, and style. Many of the musicians in this scene have now become associated with alternative country or roots rock. Stylistic origins: Punk rock, New Wave, southern rock, roots rock, country, country rock. Cultural origins: Late 1970s United Kingdom and early 1980s Los Angeles. Typical instruments: Vocals - Electric guitar - Bass - Drums - Occasional use of other instruments. Mainstream popularity: Underground, but received moderate attention in the early 1990s with Social Distortion gaining gold certifications in the U.S. Derivative forms: Alternative country. In list of notable cowpunk bands: 500 Miles to Memphis) 500 Miles to Memphis (500 Miles to Memphis is an American Cowpunk band from Cincinnati, Ohio)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Sept. 13, 2012:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "500 Miles to Memphis (Musical group). We've built up to nothing [SR] 2010.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Purveyors of cowpunk from Toronto)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yeehaa Cowboys, via Airnyc.org, Sept. 13, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yeehaa Cowboys (Musical group). Cowpunk baby, cowpunk! [SR] 1997.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cow Punk is Country Punk. Los Angeles Art-Punk pioneers X grew into a sort-of Cow Punk band as their career progressed. The Beat Farmers, Mojo Nixon, Dash Rip Rock and Social Distortion are all Cow Punk bands.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "What is cow punk?, via Punk Lesson 101 website, Sept. 13, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Country punk rock music"}}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Country punk rock music"}}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cow punk music"}}, {"@id": "_:n182d134cc6834419b72062f00c607efeb17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cow punk music"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026745"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026746", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCrunk (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026746", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb1"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Crunk (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027037"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb5"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb6"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb7"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb8"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:52"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Crunk (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Crunk music: spawned in Atlanta, with roots deeply planted in the fertile southern soil of Bass; think of it as hip-hop's version of punk or metal rock)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "About Rap/Hip-Hop WWW site, Dec. 27, 2005", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Crunk music (also spelled Krunk Muzik) is a specific type of hip hop music, based out of the southern United States, particularly on the eastern side of Atlanta, Georgia, and Memphis, Tennessee. While most crunk-style music could be called Dirty South or southern rap, the reverse is not necessarily true)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Nov. 16, 2005", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Crunk classics, p2004.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb8", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb9"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Krunk muzik"}}, {"@id": "_:ne69f16e1153841c3bfb47c9b6352ce1cb9", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Krunk muzik"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026746"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026747", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCs\u00e1rd\u00e1s (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026747", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b1"}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cs\u00e1rd\u00e1s (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b5"}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-03-11T09:56:23"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cs\u00e1rd\u00e1s (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cs\u00e1rd\u00e1s. Hungarian dance, often misspelt Czardas, in 2 parts; slow introductory lass\u00f9 followed by excited main section in duple time, friss.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 9, 2014 :", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cs\u00e1rd\u00e1s; Hungarian: , often seen with the archaic spelling Cz\u00e1rd\u00e1s, is a traditional Hungarian folk dance, the name derived from cs\u00e1rda (old Hungarian term for tavern). It originated in Hungary and was popularized by Romani music (Cig\u00e1ny) bands in Hungary and neighboring lands)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, viewed August 9, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cz\u00e1rd\u00e1s (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n6d931f457d7844d7b8c60016bbf867d2b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cz\u00e1rd\u00e1s (Music)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026747"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026748", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCuarteto (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026748", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab1"}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cuarteto (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab5"}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:52"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cuarteto (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "t.p. (Mu\u015bica de cuarteto) p. 7 (Cuarteto)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 00307724: La m\u00fasica cuartetera, 1998:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "v. 2, p. 273 (Cuarteto, m\u00fasica cuartetera; highly popular dance music \"invented\" in 1943 by the Cuarteto Leo, and the style named after the group; has an accompaniment pattern, the tunga-tunga, the characteristic and identifying feature of all cuarteto music)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Garland encyc. of world music:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "M\u00fasica cuartetera"}}, {"@id": "_:nb209514037f44b23a21557bad419015ab8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "M\u00fasica cuartetera"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026748"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026749", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCumbia (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026749", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb1"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cumbia (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb5"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb6"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb7"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb8"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:52"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cumbia (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Colombian cumbia began as many popular Latin styles began: as folklore. Dating back to the colonial period in Colombia's Atlantic (Caribbean) coast, cumbia emerged as a courtship dance and music that celebrated the union of African and indigenous people (called zambos), and went on to become one of the most popular dance styles in both South and Central America and beyond)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "National Geographic World Music online, June 9, 2011", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Cumbia cumbia [SR] : a selection of Colombian cumbia recordings, 1989.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(cumbia: an accordion-led \"vallenato\" style combining Andean Indian, African, and European elements. Hugely popular in Colombia. Key album: Cumbia cumbia cumbia (Discos Fuentes label))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Web site All Music Guide, Jan. 12, 2000", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n936fd782c92b40e695c5401248ddd6ecb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 4 of booklet (\"Today, the cumbia accounts for the vast majority of the chanchona repertoire--perhaps 80% or more--capturing the heart of the chanchona tradition.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Hermanos Lovo. Soy salvadore\u00f1o! [SR] p2011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026749"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026750", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aCumulative songs", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026750", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db1"}, {"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cumulative songs"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under [Enumerative songs]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026811"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Songs that repetitiously list a series of associated items, actions, or people, in which each stanza incorporates the words from all previous stanzas in incremental fashion. For songs that repetitiously list a series of associated items, actions, or people see [Enumerative songs.]"}, {"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-01T10:43:02"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Cumulative songs"}}, {"@id": "_:n4eeb82280c2b4e62809bf54cc2e4267db5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cumulative song; a song with a simple verse structure modified by progressive addition so that each verse is longer than the verse before)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, viewed August 29, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026750"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026751", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aD\u0101dr\u0101s", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026751", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb1"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "D\u0101dr\u0101s"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026859"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027103"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb5"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb6"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb7"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb8"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:52"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "D\u0101dr\u0101s"}}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "label, side two (Ghazals & dadra) container (Ghazals and dadras; Ghazal) liner notes (\"Her silvery rich voice and her superb expressive style were ideally suited for rendering romantic ghazals and dadras\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Ghazals and dadras / Malika Pukhraj, 1971:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Khalid Manzoor Basra. Music in Pakistan: \"Dadra - a musical genre, sung in a tal cycle of six beats stresses the words more than the musical intricacies in its rendition as opposed to the thumri, a genre of singing, light and amorous in character, which employs intricate melismatic patterns and stresses musical lines more than the words\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The South Asia web site, June 19, 2009", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"After a first generation of renowned artists ... the Pakistani preference for sung poetry has shifted artistic succession to semi-classical song, mainly ghazal, as well as \u1e6dhumr\u012b and d\u0101dr\u0101\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove Music online s.v. Pakistan, June 3, 2009", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8e9aec77b20b4fc9896852b936b602ddb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"The term d\u0101dr\u0101, aside from referring to a common six-beat cycle, also denotes a semi-classical vocal genre, closely related to \u1e6dhumr\u012b but having a somewhat lighter character. In d\u0101dr\u0101the singer generally employs D\u0101dr\u0101 or Kaharv\u0101 t\u0101la and maintains a more lively rhythmic lilt; d\u0101dr\u0101 lyrics are exclusively amatory and often include verses in Urdu as well as Braj-bh\u0101\u015b\u0101\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove Music online s.v. India, June 3, 2009", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026751"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026752", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aDance accompaniment music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026752", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b1"}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Dance accompaniment music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b5"}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Musical compositions intended or adapted for use with dance class instruction."}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-14T10:01:46"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Dance accompaniment music"}}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove dict. of music;Britannica online, WWW site, Apr. 4, 2001", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "CIP t.p. (dance accompaniment)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cavalli, Harriet. Dance and music : a guide to dance accompaniment:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ballet dance music"}}, {"@id": "_:n8b42b440b7564e5eb6514633679f8035b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ballet dance music"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026752"}
