 dansi; a non-Islamic popular music that developed in East Africa by the 1940s)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Garland encyc. of world music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58a2cef089f7464ab6f5e185e7f53e8db6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "documentation (dansi)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Perullo, A. I. Tanzania, Dar es Salaam, 2000-2002:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026756"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026757", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aDanzones (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026757", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb1"}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Danzones (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb5"}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb6"}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb7"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:52"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Danzones (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "labels (nearly every selection is designated \"Danz\u00f3n\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Danzones, 196? (Kristal KS-1120):", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(danz\u00f3n; danzones)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Diccionario de la m\u00fasica espa\u00f1ola e hispanoamericana", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne7b82e372d6d4d2a9495e033b44990fdb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"Formal ballroom couple-dance in rondo form derived from the contredanse and the habanera traditions of the 19th century, both considered part of the flowering of Cuban musical nationalism in the late colonial ... Written in 2/4 metre, it is slower, more cadenced and varied than other related forms ... African percussion textures, instrumentation and rhythms, including extensive use of symmetrical cinquillo and tresillo patterns, were staggered rhythmically to create complex instrumental cross-rhythms ... At the end of the 20th century, it was still danced in Cuba and Mexico... it formed part of the repertory of various popular musicians and orchestras who continued to compose new pieces\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online (subject entry), Sept. 4, 2009", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026757"}
