{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026896", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aKlezmer music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026896", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b1"}, {"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Klezmer music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026809"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b5"}, {"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b6"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:55"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Klezmer music"}}, {"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Klezmer music. The primarily instrumental music accompanying Jewish celebrations and rites of passage.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n36063f30a5dc4b3b9f6f537fbdcc6686b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Klezmer. From the Hebrew-Aramaic words kley (\"instrument\") and zemer (\"song\"), the Yiddishized contraction refers to a musician while the Americanized usage (\"klezmer music\") refers to a genre of Jewish music with roots in Yiddish folk traditions.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 28, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026896"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026897", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aKolos (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014026897", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b1"}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kolos (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026809"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b5"}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:55"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kolos (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "page 926, under Croatian musical culture (Calendric celebrations and work parties afforded opportunities for courtship as young people sang and danced together. Kolo, the word for dance, signifies a characteristic round dance and a village event, often held in front of the church after Sunday services, when young people sang and danced while their elders chaperoned them.) page 950 (...the central Serbian round dance in six steps (kolo u \u0161est, often called simply kolo) has effectively become the Serbian national dance among Serbs everywhere.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Garland encyclopedia of world music. Vol. 8, Europe:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Bosnia-Herzegovina 2. Rural music (The various forms of the female wedding repertory were performed by groups of girls or women. In Hercegovina, they were named kolarice after the kolo circle dance performed while singing.) under Yugoslavia. III, Traditional music. 1. Serbia (Ethnochoreographers have recorded a large number of folk dances in Serbia. These include regionally differing kolos with different choreography, with odd or even beats. Their names usually relate to the manner of dance, origin or region where they are to be found)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 28, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kolarice (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0979c953e038471e9ebaf24b8dcbdd60b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kolarice (Music)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026897"}
