 "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "CIP galley (rap songs)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Watkins, W.H. All you need to know about rappin', c1984:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(rap)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Rolling Stone encyc. of rock & roll, c1983", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(rap)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove dict. of American music, c1986", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(rap: predominantly African-American musical style that first gained prominence in the late 1970s; characterized by semi-spoken rhymes declaimed over a rhythmic musical backing, drawn from the sampling of pre-existing recordings and the use of DJ mixing techniques)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove, 2nd ed. WWW site, Jan. 29, 2001", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rappin' (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rappin' (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rapping (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rapping (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rap songs"}}, {"@id": "_:naf023882be974ba9890a23d784683067b19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rap songs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027037"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027038", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aRappresentazioni sacre (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014027038", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b1"}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rappresentazioni sacre (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026775"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027062"}], "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027081"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b5"}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-23T11:19:29"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rappresentazioni sacre (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 99391966: Schmelzer, J.H. St\u00e4rcke der Lieb, c1998: introd. (sepolcro, also called rappresentazione sacra)", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove (rappresentazione sacra; sacra rappresentazione; plural: rappresentazioni sacre; the term was used in the 15th and 16th centuries to designate a kind of religious play with music in the Italian language cultivated chiefly in Florence; a significant forerunner of both opera and oratorio; during the second half of the 17th century in Vienna the term was often applied to the sepolcro)", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sacre rappresentazioni (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n4a96c533f20244d7ad283473bb11eb04b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sacre rappresentazioni (Music)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027038"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027039", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aRapso", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014027039", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b1"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rapso"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b5"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b6"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b7"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b8"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:58"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rapso"}}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Rapso: This genre is quite recent, emerging about twenty five years ago. However, it draws on the ancient African tradition of story telling. Rapso is street poetry. Its main theme is the issues that affect the lives of ordinary people. Rapso may be unaccompanied or accompanied by a simple ensemble or full orchestration.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "TriniMusic.com, via WWW, Aug. 2, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(What is Rapso? There is a popular myth that rapso is the fusion of American rap music with soca ... but not true. Rapso is a unique style of street poetry from Trinidad and Tobago that originated in the the 1970's ... Lancelot Layne's 1970 hit Blow away was the first rapso recording)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Caribbean Music 101, via WWW, Aug. 1, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Rapso is a style of dup-poetry soca - the energetic and disco-influenced party music descended from calypso)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "All Music Guide, via WWW, Aug. 1, 2003", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5c4605f6b8764b199b121dbd80ea62f9b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "insert (Brother Resistance is one of the founding members and the driving force of the new Caribbean musical style called rapso. Rapso is the rap of soca, the poetry of calypso, highlighting the traditional African rhythms of the Caribbean ... the combination of voice rhythm with traditional drum and steel drum.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Brother Resistance. When de riddum explode [SR] p2002:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027039"}
