ewhere ca. 1840)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027042"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027043", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aReels (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014027043", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb1"}, {"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Reels (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027114"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:58"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Reels (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n470cef3e07a84be68233df8356c9ff1bb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Reel. A dance for couples, usually four to eight, documented in Scotland as early as the 16th century... Its music is in a moderately fast duple meter... A related dance in a slower tempo is the strathspey)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027043"}
