 the Dead (Missa pro defunctis), called Requiem after the first word of its introit... The term has also been used in the 20th century in works not strictly liturgical but written in honor of the dead...)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027048"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027049", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aResponses (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014027049", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b1"}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Responses (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026707"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027062"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b5"}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-02-13T13:06:58"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Responses (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Responsory (A category of Western chant serving at Matins and monastic Vespers as musical postludes to the reading of lessons, as the gradual and alleluia do at the Mass. Indeed, responsories make up the greater part of Matins, and in the total repertory of Roman chant are surpassed in quantity only by Office antiphons. The responsories of the Office (like the gradual and alleluia of the Mass) are termed responsorial chants because in them choir responds with a refrain to verses sung by a cantor. In method of delivery they are clearly related to responsorial psalmody, although it is important that a distinction be maintained between the more ancient practice of responsorial psalm singing and the specific liturgical genre that bears its name.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed May 28, 2014 :", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(In Anglican church, the replies of the choir (or congregation) to the versicles of the priest. Usually in plainsong)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed May 28, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Responsories"}}, {"@id": "_:n6f01716605014fbf8ac7569449a87d04b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Responsories"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027049"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027050", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aRevues", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014027050", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab1"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Revues"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under [Musicals; Music theater]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026775"}, "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2016026052"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026100"}], "madsrdf:hasReciprocalAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026939"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab5"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab6"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab7"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab8"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab9"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab10"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab11"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab12"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab15"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab18"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab21"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab24"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Theatrical productions from around the end of the 18th century that feature a series of songs, dances, and other entertainments without any unifying dramatic element. For musical/theatrical productions consisting of musical numbers integrated into a dramatic framework see Musicals. For musical works, often small in scale and primarily of the 20th century, that combine elements of music, drama, and sometimes dance in unconventional ways that result in works distinct from traditional forms see Music theater."}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-26T14:29:46"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wimtmla"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Revues"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Herman, J. Jerry's girls [SR] p1984.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Revue)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove dict. of American music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Musical shows)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LC database, Oct. 21, 1996", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Revue)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Harvard dict. of music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Under Revue (developed in France during the 19th century, was taken up by other countries including Britain and the USA, and enjoyed its greatest acclaim and significance between the world wars) under Table entertainment (A peculiarly British species of performance, consisting generally of a mixture of narration and singing delivered by a single individual seated behind a table facing the audience ... From 1789 to 1809 Charles Dibdin gave a series of table entertainments in London in which song was the prominent feature. Dibdin united in himself the functions of author, composer, narrator, singer and accompanist. Impersonations were added by comedians who took up the genre, which had much in common with the techniques of music hall in the Victorian period.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove dict. of mus. WWW site, Jun. 16, 2011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Revue (A topical, satirical show consisting of a series of scenes and episodes, usually having a central theme but not a dramatic plot, with spoken verse and prose, sketches, songs, dances, ballet and speciality acts. In revue there are elements of other stage forms such as cabaret, variety show, vaudeville, pantomime, burlesque and musical comedy.) under Vaudeville (At the turn of the century in the USA vaudeville achieved great popularity with its combination of songs, dances, pretty girls, rapid-fire comics, skits and acrobatics. Such variety shows are still popular, though less common.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove dict. of mus. WWW site, Feb. 14, 2007:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Boardman, G. American musical revue, c1985.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety shows (Musical theater)"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Variety shows (Musical theater)"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Musical revues"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Musical revues"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Vaudeville shows"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Vaudeville shows"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Musical shows"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Musical shows"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab24", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab25"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Table entertainments"}}, {"@id": "_:n52cf1ce1156b45ffaaa70eaa26b9b08ab25", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Table entertainments"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027050"}
