"madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Siciliana, siciliano [It., Eng, Ger.; Fr. Sicilienne; Sp. Siciliana]. (1). A late Baroque instrumental movement or an aria that evokes a gentle pastoral mood..., usually through slow 6 /8 or 12 /8 time and simple phrases with repeated dotted figures... It frequently appears as a slow movement in sonatas and dance suites... and was considered to be a sort of slow gigue, though little is known of it as an actual dance.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne3eeb4a92a3e448f9791e6813189e677b6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ne3eeb4a92a3e448f9791e6813189e677b7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Siciliennes (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:ne3eeb4a92a3e448f9791e6813189e677b7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Siciliennes (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:ne3eeb4a92a3e448f9791e6813189e677b9", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ne3eeb4a92a3e448f9791e6813189e677b10"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sicilianos (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:ne3eeb4a92a3e448f9791e6813189e677b10", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Sicilianos (Music)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027090"}
