e": "Timba (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n00aaa5ea36ba41e0adca3831a0e2fa7bb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Timba is the Cuban variant of salsa music, and is often understood to be a sub-category of salsa. However, the historical development of timba has been quite independent of the development of salsa in the United States and Puerto Rico and the music has its own trademark aspects)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, July 3, 2006", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n00aaa5ea36ba41e0adca3831a0e2fa7bb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "sticker (timba)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: What you've been waiting for = Lo que esperabas, p2006:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n00aaa5ea36ba41e0adca3831a0e2fa7bb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "All-music guide, July 3, 2006", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n00aaa5ea36ba41e0adca3831a0e2fa7bb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Cuban salsa, Timba combines elements of traditional Cuban music, salsa, jazz, rock and hip hop)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "timba.com, July 3, 2006", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027139"}
