: "en", "@value": "(Vocal music popular in Venice and Padua during the early 16th century; 4 voices, refrain, includes nonsense syllables lilolela; some are quodlibets of popular song texts and tunes)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Harvard dict. of mus.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027161"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027162", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aVirelais (Formes fixes)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2014027162", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b1"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Virelais (Formes fixes)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027103"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b5"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b6"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b7"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b8"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b10"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b13"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2014-12-10T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-02-13T09:39:35"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Virelais (Formes fixes)"}}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Virelay, also virelai; an old French verse form having a refrain and composed wholly in two rhymes; an old song or poem)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Web. 3", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Virelai; one of the three formes fixes, prominent in the poetry and music of France in the 14th and 15th centuries; pl. virelais)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Harvard dict. of music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Ensemble Project Ars Nova. Ars magis subtiliter [SR] p1989.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Bergerette (i) ... (2) In common parlance the word is often used to denote a virelai setting from the second half of the 15th century, in the erroneous belief that its single-stanza form is not found among virelais of the 14th century. In this sense it is treated as a forme fixe (see Formes fixes); and the word appears to lie at the root of the Italian word Barzelletta, which does (in music) denote a forme fixe.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed, Aug. 12, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Virelai. One of the three formes fixes (the others are the ballade and the rondeau) that dominated French song and poetry in the 14th and 15th centuries. Its musical structure is essentially ABBA, regardless of subtleties of rhythm and metre in the superimposed text. The virelai form has a long and complex history, closely interwoven with the general history of early song and dance... Its principal features were: the first musical section for the refrain, several lines in length; two sets of matching text for the repeated second musical section, usually with first-time (Ouvert) and second-time (clos) bars; the return to the first musical section with text to match the rhyme and metre of the refrain; and finally the repetition of the refrain itself. The refrain always comes at the close, even if the whole form is to be gone through two or three times, as often happens. In such a case the composition may be very extended and far more substantial than it appears in its written form (as is also true for the ballade and the rondeau.))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 4, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Virelays (Formes fixes)"}}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Virelays (Formes fixes)"}}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bergerettes (Virelais)"}}, {"@id": "_:n70151479f60b45cd82176e6aa35fe707b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bergerettes (Virelais)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027162"}
