8aae5b6f2d4fd1b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Score (i) (A 'piano score' is an arrangement for solo piano of any ensemble composition...)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 28, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n497c9eb39797427db98aae5b6f2d4fd1b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Piano score. A score of a work for orchestra or other ensemble arranged on two staves in the fashion of piano music, sometimes with indications of the instruments intended for salient parts)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n497c9eb39797427db98aae5b6f2d4fd1b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Piano score. A reduction of an instrumental work or a vocal work with instruments to a version for piano. May include the words of a vocal work)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "RDA toolkit, viewed August 28, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027205"}
