cies UF Prophetic writings; Omen texts)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Religion genre/form terms: information gathered on behalf of the Library of Congress... American Theological Library Association, et. al, c2012:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n27aa1f4275ed4031a15a045ca2c38d3cb6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n27aa1f4275ed4031a15a045ca2c38d3cb7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Omens"}}, {"@id": "_:n27aa1f4275ed4031a15a045ca2c38d3cb7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Omens"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026059"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026060", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPaper dolls", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026060", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb1"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Paper dolls"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026111"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb5"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb6"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb7"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb8"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb9"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-06-15T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-12-13T15:12:16"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Paper dolls"}}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Paper dolls. BT Dolls. BT Paper toys. RT Paper work)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, Sept. 1, 2016", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "unnumbered page 2 (paper doll sets are suitable for framing)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Hendricks, Donald. Jane Austen's Emma : a paper doll, 2000?:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(A paper doll is a two-dimensional figure drawn or printed on paper for which accompanying clothing has also been made. It may be a figure of a person, animal or inanimate object. The term may be extended to include similar items made of materials other than paper, such as plastic, cloth or wood. The term also may include three-dimensional dolls and their costumes that are made exclusively of paper. Collectors sometimes extend their collections to include other toys printed on paper, such as paper airplanes, cars and trains, animals and birds, villages, furniture and so on.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Johnson, J.M. History of paper dolls, c1999, via OPDAG [Original Paper Doll Artists Guild] website, Sept. 1, 2016", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(paper doll: A graphic work consisting of an articulated or unarticulated human or animal figure drawn or printed on paper or cardboard, with multiple parts or costumes, usually issued on a single sheet or in a booklet, intended to be cut out and used as a toy. The first manufactured paper dolls were issued in London in 1810 and in Boston in 1812. By the 1820s boxed sets of paper dolls were commercially available in Europe. The first celebrity paper doll, issued in the 1830s, was of the renowned ballerina Marie Taglioni.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary for library and information science, Sept. 1, 2016", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb9", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb10"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Dolls, Paper"}}, {"@id": "_:n4733c9d30a0d468c939ec3b0992f48abb10", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Dolls, Paper"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026060"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026061", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aRhyme royal", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026061", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b1"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rhyme royal"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026383"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b5"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b6"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b7"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b8"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b9"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b10"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b11"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b12"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b13"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b16"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b19"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-06-19T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-12-13T15:12:17"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rhyme royal"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Rhyme Royal. A seven-line pentameter stanza rhyming ababbcc, one of many complex stanzas developed in the late Middle Ages; sometimes called the Troilus stanza, after Chaucer's use of it in Troilus and Criseyde)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The Princeton encyclopedia of poetry and poetics, \u00a92012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Gregory, Harold Anthony. Concord revisited : an epic poem of the Americas in three cantos, in three languages, in rime royal, \u00a91972.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(rhyme royal. A stanza form consisting of seven 5-stress lines (iambic pentameters) rhyming ababbcc, first used by Chaucer and thus also known as the Chaucerian stanza; continued to be an important form of English verse in the 15th and 16th centuries)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Baldick, C. The Oxford dict. of literary terms, 2008", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "foreword (the rime royal form) p. 82 (Chaucer is credited with introducing this seven-lined stanza of iambic pentameter into our poetry; it was also used by Hoccleve, Lydgate, Henryson, Dunbar and Sackville. Shakespeare chose rime royal for The Rape of Lucrece)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Corringham, Mary. I, Jane Austen : a re-creation in rime royal based on the letters of Jane Austen, her novels and the comments of her biographers, 1971:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Rhyme royal (or Rime royal) is a rhyming stanza form that was introduced into English poetry by Geoffrey Chaucer. The rhyme royal stanza consists of seven lines, usually in iambic pentameter. The rhyme scheme is a-b-a-b-b-c-c. In practice, the stanza can be constructed either as a tercet and two couplets (a-b-a, b-b, c-c) or a quatrain and a tercet (a-b-a-b, b-c-c). This allows for variety, especially when the form is used for longer narrative poems. Along with the couplet, it was the standard narrative metre in the late Middle Ages.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, June 19, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Rhyme Royal (or Rime Royal). A seven-lined iambic pentameter stanza rhyming ababbcc, sometimes with an alexandrine (hexameter) seventh line. Rhyme royal enjoys the unique distinction of being the only stanza used by all three poets customarily called the greatest in English--Chaucer, Shakespeare, and Milton--as well as by Wordsworth and Auden)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harmon W. A handbook to literature, c2009", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(classic Rime Royal form, a rhyme scheme of iambic pentameter in a pattern of A B A B B C C)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "A tribute in rime : I, Jane Austen, by Mary Corringham, reviewed by Diana Birchall, in JASNA news, spring 2002, viewed online June 19, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Rhyme Royal. A stanza of seven decasyllabic lines rhyming ababbcc, first used in Eng. by Chaucer in Troilus and Criseyde (hence its alternate name, \"Troilus stanza\"), The Parlement of Foules, and four of the Canterbury Tales, formed on the model of 7-line stanzas in the lyrics of Machaut and Deschamps, or by dropping the fifth line of the ottava rima stanza (abababcc; q.v.) as in Boccaccio, or perhaps as a variety of the chant royal (q.v.), a festive form of poetry often composed for the puy, a guild festival that flourished in France and England from the late 13th c. well into Chaucer's time. The puy traditionally elected a \"prince\" who presided over mock royal feasts and who crowned the chauncon reale as the prize-winning poem of the occasion. The r. r. stanza was also used in ceremonies for the entry of royalty into a city. Later examples survive--John Lydgate's civic show in honor of Henry V's return to London in 1432, and the festive entry of Henry VII into York in 1486. Hence, r. r. apparently had its origin in events that honored royalty both real and imaginary, a form it continued to take both directly and as a literary artifice in the poetry of Chaucer, whose Parlement of Foules has been widely regarded as an occasional poem in honor of Richard II. ... R. r. in Chaucer is, however, a remarkably flexible form, used as widely and imaginatively as the couplet, in every sort of poetic context. Ample enough for narrative purposes, the stanza is also suited to description, digression, comment, and literary burlesque. It dominated Eng. poetry in the 15th c., being used widely in the poetry of Lydgate, Hoccleve, Dunbar, Henryson, Hawes, and Barclay, as well as in the drama of Skelton and Bale. As late as the second half of the 16th c., r. r. was the chief Eng. stanza for serious verse, as in Spenser's Foure Hymnes and Shakespeare's Rape of Lucrece. But Michael Drayton's revision of his r. r. narrative Mortimeriados into ottava rima (as The Barron's Wars) sometime before 1619 signaled the end of r. r. as a great Eng. measure. In modern times it has been essayed by Wordsworth (\"Resolution and Independence\"), Morris (Earthly Paradise), Auden (Letter to Lord Byron), and Masefield; Theodore Roethke adapts the rhyme scheme to ababccc for \"I Knew a Woman.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The new Princeton encyclopedia of poetry and poetics, 1993", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Chaucerian stanzas"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Chaucerian stanzas"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rime royal"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rime royal"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b19", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b20"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Troilus stanzas"}}, {"@id": "_:nfda1ba8e4be74aebb65371031f05de46b20", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Troilus stanzas"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026061"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026062", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aComing-of-age drama", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026062", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb1"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Coming-of-age drama"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026297"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb5"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb6"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb7"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb8"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb9"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb10"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb11"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb12"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-12-13T15:12:16"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-06-22T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Coming-of-age drama"}}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Breitkopf, F.D. Faust : ein Bildungsdrama, 2011.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Armstead, C.M. Blooming in the whirlwind : a black woman's coming of age drama with incidental music, 1997.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Scholl, M. German \"Bildungsdrama\": Schiller's Don Carlos, Geothe's Torquato Tasso, and Kleist's Prinz Friedrich von Homburg, 1973.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Merriam-Webster online dictionary, Nov. 7, 2016: (Bildungsdrama not found);Collins Dictionary online, Nov. 7, 2016: (Bildungsdrama not found);OED online, Nov. 7, 2016: (Bildungsdrama not found)", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 11 (There is a type of drama for which the designation \"Bildungsdrama\" is appropriate. This drama came into being at the same time as the Bildungsroman, i.e. in the last part of the eighteenth century ... After he had been presented in the Storm and Stress drama in his unrestrained adolescence, the figure of the Young Man began to undergo a maturation process. In the \"Bildungsdrama\" this process forms the substance of the dramatic plot.) p. 12 (The main distinguishing features between the \"Bildungsdrama\" and the \"Bildungsroman\" are concentration of plot, limitation of experience, and the rapidity with which the character growth takes place. As in the novel, the dramatic hero learns primarily from life itself, although there are leadership figures present.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Scholl, M. The Bildungsdrama of the age of Goethe, 1976:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "t.p. (translated with notes by Hilary Collier Sy-Quia; adapted in verse drama by Peter Oswald)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Schiller, F. Don Carlos, 1996:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "table of contents (Coming-of-age on the rez : William S. Yellow Robe's The independence of Eddie Rose as Native American bildungsdrama / David Krasner)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "American Indian Workshop (23rd : 2002 : Dublin, Ireland). Native American performance and representation, 2011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bildungsdrama"}}, {"@id": "_:ncef7a8b78f934cc8a047beb391c88ffcb13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bildungsdrama"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026062"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026063", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aUtopian poetry", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026063", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab1"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Utopian poetry"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026481"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab5"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab6"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab7"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab8"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab9"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab10"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab11"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab12"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab13"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Poems that depict an ideal community or society."}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2017-01-09T09:18:12"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-08-20T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Utopian poetry"}}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Utopian poetry (Utopian poetry, poetry that describes a utopia or any sort of utopian ideal. Sir Thomas More's Utopia (1516)--the first printed work to use the term utopia, derived from the Greek words for \"not\" (ou) and \"place\" (topos)--is for many specialists the major starting point of utopian prose. The same claim can be made for utopian poetry, as the first strictly \"utopian\" poems appeared within More's text. The first of these is \"A Specimen of Utopian Poetry\"; the second, \"Lines on the Island of Utopia by the Poet Laureate, Mr. Windbag Nonsenso's Sister's Son,\" is a brief satirical poem believed to be a gibe at John Skelton. ... the history of utopian poetry is often inextricably bound up with its dystopian opposite, as in Edgar Allan Poe's \"Eldorado\" (1849). Many utopian poems herald the coming of a new Golden Age or a paradise-like place (Percy Bysshe Shelley's Hellas [1822] or Oscar Wilde's \"Pan: A Villanelle\" [1880]); others express a regret for a pagan paradise lost (Friedrich Schiller's influential \"Die G\u00f6tter Griechenlandes\" [1788; \"The Gods of Greece\"]). ... In contemporary poetry, the genre has for decades remained a productive one. Just two examples, from the 1970s, are \"To the Thin and Elegant Woman Who Resides Inside of Alix Nelson\" (1976), Diane Wakoski's provocative imagining of renewed sexual plenitude in a New World America, and Derek Walcott's satirical poem \"New World\" (1976), which offers a mordant view of utopian colonization by parodying the biblical motif of the Garden of Eden. Although it may seem that utopian prose works are more centrally political in nature and utopian poems more essentially lyrical and fanciful, much utopian poetry is deeply concerned with concrete efforts toward achieving a better world. This tendency is particularly apparent in British utopian poetry of the Romantic and Victorian periods, much of which focuses on denouncing the ills of industrialism.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Britannica online, Aug. 20, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "M\u00e9ndez Rubio, A. Poes\u00eda y utop\u00eda, 1999.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 9 (students recited Utopic poetry from Walt Whitman, Li Bai, Rumi, and others)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Montgomery College. College bulletin, May 2013, viewed online Aug. 20, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "table of contents (Utopian poetry)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Viable utopian ideas, \u00a92003:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Weir, C.B. The utopian impulse and English romantic poetry, 1993.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Oliveira Martins, J.A. de. Utopias : versos, 1889.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 27 (H\u00f6lderlin's utopic poetry)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Whistler, D. The production of transparency : H\u00f6lderlinian practices, via WWW, viewed Aug. 20, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Finkelstein, N. The utopian moment in contemporary American poetry, \u00a91988.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Utopic poetry"}}, {"@id": "_:n15b757ff41b542c0ac66189426683beab14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Utopic poetry"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026063"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026065", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aIndie pop music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026065", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab1"}, {"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Indie pop music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026632"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab5"}, {"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab6"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Indie pop music"}}, {"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "ecip galley (Very definitely apart from indie-rock, indie-pop began life as a notion of punk that maintained some of punk's primary characteristics -- back-to-basics instrumentation (guitar, bass, drums, maybe some rudimentary keyboards), the ranking of enthusiasm and character above technical skill -- but replaced punk's anger and discordance with melody and romanticism)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: 2015013367: White, M., Popkiss: the life and afterlife of Sarah Records, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nbefedf9e36e54e87bb3c52e2168eaa1ab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Indie pop; genre of alternative rock music that originated in the United Kingdom in the mid-1980s, with its roots in Scottish post-punk bands on the Postcard Records label in the early 1980s (Josef K and Orange Juice) and the dominant UK independent band of the mid-1980s, the Smiths. Indie pop was inspired by punk's DIY ethic and related ideologies, and it generated a thriving fanzine, label, and club and gig circuit. Indie pop differs from indie rock to the extent that it is more melodic, less abrasive, and relatively angst-free)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, Apr. 3, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026065"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026067", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aBellydance music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026067", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b1"}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bellydance music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b5"}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Musical compositions composed or arranged for belly dancing."}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-07T11:11:24"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bellydance music"}}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Belly dance of Bellydance is a Western-coined name for \"solo, improvised dances based on torso articulation\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, viewed August 28, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Abdel Al, Bashir. Modern bellydance music from Arabia, p2006.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Belly dance music"}}, {"@id": "_:nc9d39789e4a347b686fff071571d6d20b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Belly dance music"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026067"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026068", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aBenediction of the Blessed Sacrament (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026068", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb1"}, {"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Benediction of the Blessed Sacrament (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026795"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027062"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Benediction of the Blessed Sacrament (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n0821c9967f01461a8dc46d03ba283bdcb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(In the Roman rite, a ceremony comprising the exposition and veneration of the Sacred Host, the singing of hymns and a blessing of the faithful with the Host. It is not part of the Mass in the strict sense... The chant prescribed for Benediction is Tantum ergo, but the detail of the service is variable and many other eucharistic chants are customary; there 250 chants in the Cantus selecti ad benedictionem (Paris, 1963), and vernacular hymns have been used for it too.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 9, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026068"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026069", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aHunting music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026069", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b1"}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hunting music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026821"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b5"}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "This term is used as a genre/form term for music surrounding the ritual of the hunt, including music used to coordinate and rally the hunt while in process."}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hunting music"}}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Jagdmusik (The German application of the term denotes the entire code of musical signals for the hunt, but more particularly that body of harmonic hunting music which relates specifically to the horn...)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 11, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Music of the hunt, 1967.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Jagdmusik"}}, {"@id": "_:nd022c3dafabd4d408dbcacdd7e9c54a7b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Jagdmusik"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026069"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026070", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aJ\u00f9j\u00fa music", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026070", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b1"}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "J\u00f9j\u00fa music"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b5"}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b6"}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b7"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "J\u00f9j\u00fa music"}}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Juju music)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Hennepin", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "CIP data (juju; juju music; popular music of Nigerian Yoruba)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Waterman, C.A. J\u00f9j\u00fa, 1990:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n58ae91ffb1b44e4c839cec85efce06f8b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(African popular music genre performed by the Yoruba of south-west Nigeria. J\u00f9j\u00fa music combines indigenous praise-singing and proverbs, the flowing rhythms of social dance drumming and the traditional rhetorical role of the Yoruba talking drum with a variety of foreign influences, including electric guitars and synthesizers, African American soul music, country and western music and themes from Indian film music...A contemporary j\u00f9j\u00fa band comprises three main sections made up of singers, percussionists and guitarists. The singers stand in a line at the front of the band; the praise-singer or 'band captain' stands in the middle, flanked on either side by chorus singers. The percussion section includes from one to three talking drums, several conga drums, a set of bongos played with light sticks ('double toy'), a shekere bottle gourd rattle, maracas and an agogo iron bell. Larger and well-financed bands may also include 'jazz drums' (a trap set). These large bands help to boost the reputation of patrons who hire them to perform at parties; they play a role in sustaining an idealized image of Yoruba society as a flexible hierarchy.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed Aug. 12, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026070"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026071", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aKwaito", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026071", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb1"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kwaito"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb5"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb6"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb7"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb8"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb9"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kwaito"}}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Kwaito WWW site, Oct. 23, 2000.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: TKZee Family (Musical group). Guz 20001, p1999.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "title of article (Quiet kwaito)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The Star Tonight, Sept. 26, 2000:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "music dict. (kwaito: South African urban music of the post-apartheid era. Specifically part of the urban black youth experience, kwaito takes as its foundation slowed down house beats)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Click2music WWW site, Oct. 23, 2000:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n98ef2b4410b64438a5d8dc030177888bb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Bubblegum (In the mid-1990s the township dance music market was taken over by kwaito (a South Africanized blend of hip hop with European and American house, pop and techno) in which the latest township catch phrases are sung and chanted over computer-generated backing. Top kwaito groups include Boom Shaka, Arthur, Trompies and Bongo Maffin.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed Aug. 12, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026071"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026073", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMa\u02bbaravot", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026073", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b1"}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ma\u02bbaravot"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027181"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b5"}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b7"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ma\u02bbaravot"}}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Lel shimurim, 1300?", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Ma\u02bbaravot (also ma\u02bbaravim, sing. ma\u02bbaravit), arrangement of piyutim that embellish the Ma\u02bbariv (\u02bbArvit) prayers for festivals and special Sabbaths)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Encyc. Jud., 1972", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ma\u02bbaravim"}}, {"@id": "_:n9adc859fbc774aef8dedfe10fcee2d59b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ma\u02bbaravim"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026073"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026074", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMinnesang", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026074", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b1"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Minnesang"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027103"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b5"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b6"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b7"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b8"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b10"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Minnesang"}}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(The German tradition of courtly lyric and secular monophony that flourished particularly in the 12th, 13th and 14th centuries. Though it is in many ways merely the German branch of the genre represented by the troubadours and trouv\u00e8res in France, it has substantial independent features. The musical history of Minnesang is a particularly controversial subject because the melodies survive largely in manuscripts from the 14th and 15th centuries)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed Aug. 12, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Minnesang)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Grove", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: McMahon, J.V. The music of the early Minnesang, c1990.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Minnesong; minnesang)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Web. 3", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Minnesang)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Harvard dict. mus.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Minnesong"}}, {"@id": "_:nd1767d179e124fc28825c78bf5ed5491b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Minnesong"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026074"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026075", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPlenas", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026075", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab1"}, {"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Plenas"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027103"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab5"}, {"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab6"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "The Puerto Rican song and dance-music form that combines European and African characteristics."}, {"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-02-08T16:27:02"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Plenas"}}, {"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(A song genre of Puerto Rico. It is believed to have originated in the early 20th century, with a binary form consisting of solo or duet melodies followed by choral refrains. Narrative texts, often humorous, contain social commentary. The plena is characterized by extensive syncopation, while the use of triplet figures in vocal lines creates rhythmic contrast with the duple metre accompaniment of guitars, panderetas (tambourines) and conga drums and, more recently, orchestras with extended percussion sections.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed Aug. 12, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n2b866ae6beb6435b8e42e49c57d4621ab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "((1). Plena. A Puerto Rican song and dance-music form of both folk and popular traditions, combining European- and African-derived stylistic features... (2). In the Dominican Republic, a variety of work song, distinct from the plena of Puerto Rico)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 4th ed.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026075"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026076", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aTamboritos", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026076", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b1"}, {"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Tamboritos"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026753"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-10-28T13:03:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Tamboritos"}}, {"@id": "_:n5f2346e3df2c49bb8259bb6a578d4061b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(An Afro-Hispanic recreational dance of Panama. It is sung responsorially by women, solo or in chorus. It is accompanied by hand-clapping in duple metre and a drum ensemble including repicador, llamador, pujador, tambor, almirez and the small tamborito from which the dance gets its name. Song texts are often in copla (four-line stanza) form and express the exuberance of the Panamanian coste\u00f1o, serving also as a vehicle for socio-political commentary.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed Aug. 12, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026076"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026077", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aOrgan masses", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026077", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab1"}, {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Organ masses"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under [Masses]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026639"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027062"}], "madsrdf:hasReciprocalAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026926"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab5"}, "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab6"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Collections of versets for the organ that replace parts of the Ordinary and Proper of the Mass and are played in alternation with the sung portions. For musical settings of the Mass in its entirety or for the Mass ordinary see [Masses.]"}, {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-01T11:28:21"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-04T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/castsmf"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Organ masses"}}, {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(A collection of versets for the organ replacing parts of the Ordinary and Proper of the Mass and played in alternation with the sung portions. The term Alternatim is frequently used to describe the practice of dividing sections of a liturgical text between organ and choir. The choir normally sings a plainchant setting of the Mass when alternating with the organ. The practice belongs almost exclusively to the liturgy of the Roman Catholic Church. The extant literature of organ masses covers most of Western Christendom and some 500 years of music history, beginning about 1400 with the organ versets in I-FZc 117 and ending late in the 19th century...."}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed Aug. 12, 2015", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Instrumental masses"}}, {"@id": "_:n3984924c83f545b8844a86e3c0344d9ab7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Instrumental masses"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026077"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026078", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aBreviaries", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026078", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b1"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Breviaries"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026039"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b5"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b6"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b7"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b10"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b13"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-28T10:54:08"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Breviaries"}}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "divine office (the daily office for the canonical hours of prayer; especially breviary 2b) breviary (2a: an ecclesiastical book containing the daily public or canonical prayers for the canonical hours; 2b: the canonical prayers for each day)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Merriam Webster online, Sept. 8, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Liturgy of the Hours (The Liturgy of the Hours, also known as the Divine Office or the Work of God; the daily prayer of the Church; each of the five canonical Hours includes selections from the Psalms that culminate in a scriptural proclamation; most important Hours are Morning and Evening Prayer, which each include a Gospel canticle; Morning and Evening Prayer also include intercessions that flow from the scriptural proclamation just as the Psalms prepare for it) National Conference of Catholic Airport Chaplains Aug. 2013 newsletter (Liturgy of the Hours (Breviary))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "United States Conference of Catholic Bishops WWW site, Sept. 8, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b7", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b8"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Divine Office (Breviaries)"}}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b8", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Divine Office (Breviaries)"}}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Liturgy of the Hours"}}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Liturgy of the Hours"}}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hours, Liturgy of the"}}, {"@id": "_:n427525dfefcb466ab91c695154ae8764b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hours, Liturgy of the"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026078"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026079", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPsalms", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026079", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb1"}, {"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Psalms"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under [Psalters]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026503"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Sacred songs originally contained in the Book of Psalms. For collections of psalms arranged for devotional or liturgical use see [Psalters.]"}, {"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-01T11:26:04"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Psalms"}}, {"@id": "_:n6bf10475ae2d4b5eba4f4d9dc8fc301cb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "psalm (1a: Any of the sacred songs contained in the Book of Psalms in the Old Testament and Hebrew Scriptures; a version or paraphrase of any of these, esp. as sung or said in public or private worship. (Now the usual sense.) 2: gen. (esp. in biblical use). A sacred song that is or may be sung in religious worship. Later also: any song or poem of a sacred or serious nature.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "OED online, Sept. 8, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026079"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026080", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPsalters", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026080", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b1"}, {"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Psalters"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under [Psalms]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026039"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026057"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b5"}, {"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b6"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Collections of psalms arranged for devotional or liturgical use. For sacred songs originally contained in the Book of Psalms see [Psalms.]"}, {"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-01T11:26:31"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Psalters"}}, {"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "psalter (1: A collection of psalms. 1a: The Book of Psalms of the Old Testament and Hebrew Scriptures. 1b: A particular translation or arrangement (prose or metrical) of the Book of Psalms. Now usu. with distinguishing word, as Latin, English, metrical, etc. 1c: A copy of, or a volume containing, the Psalms, esp. as arranged for liturgical or devotional use. 4: Any of several Irish chronicles chiefly written in verse, dating from around the 10th cent., and now no longer extant. Usu. with distinguishing word, as Psalter of Cashel, Psalter of Tara, etc.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "OED online, Sept. 8, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n70db2fc731c044feb2a4d1065fcb62f2b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "psalter (1. a translation or version of the Psalms; 2. a book containing the Psalms separately printed or especially arranged for liturgical or devotional use)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Merriam Webster online, Sept. 8, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026080"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026081", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPapal encyclicals", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026081", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b1"}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Papal encyclicals"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026044"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026047"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b5"}, "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b6"}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b9"}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b12"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Formal pastoral letters written by the Roman Catholic pope for the entire Church."}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-12-14T17:51:18"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Papal encyclicals"}}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "encyclical (A formal pastoral letter written by the pope for the entire Church. It is, first, a papal letter and is therefore distinguished from pastoral letters written by an ordinary for his diocese. It is, second, a letter and is therefore distinguished from other papal documents, such as briefs, bulls, rescripts, and constitutions. It is, third, pastoral and hence pertains ordinarily to doctrinal, moral, or disciplinary matters. It is, finally, written for the universal Church and is therefore distinguished from papal autograph letters, those written in the pope's hand, and encyclical epistles addressed only to parts of the universal Church)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "New Catholic encyclopedia, 1981:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Encyclicals, Papal"}}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Encyclicals, Papal"}}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b9", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b10"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Letters, Papal"}}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b10", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Letters, Papal"}}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Papal letters"}}, {"@id": "_:na4189143cfd742dfb10961fceec4f168b13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Papal letters"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026081"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026082", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPapal blessings", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026082", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb1"}, {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Papal blessings"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026044"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb5"}, "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb6"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-28T10:54:09"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Papal blessings"}}, {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Information about Applying for Papal Blessing Parchments: The Apostolic Blessing is granted for the following occasions: 1. Baptism, First Communion, Confirmation 2. Marriage 3. Priestly Ordination 4. Religious Profession 5. Secular Consecration 6. Ordinations of Permanent Deacons 7. Marriage Anniversaries (10, 25, 40, 50, 60 years), Priestly Ordination, Religious Profession 8. Birthdays (18, 50, 60, 70, 80, 90, 100) 9. Catholic individuals or families (with name and surname of the spouses united in a religious marriage).)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Office of Papal Charities, Vatican City, WWW site, Sept. 8, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Blessings, Papal"}}, {"@id": "_:n4d9b0b49b9f445758b5aa40432a38aefb7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Blessings, Papal"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026082"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026083", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aRosaries (Prayer books)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026083", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b1"}, {"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rosaries (Prayer books)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026049"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026057"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b5"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-28T10:54:09"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-15T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rosaries (Prayer books)"}}, {"@id": "_:nddab5cb1b7c544e7bf3771ce93452133b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "rosary (def. 5: Freq. with capital initial. Used in the title of a book of devotion, formerly freq. one incorporating the rosary (in sense 6a)) def. 6a (orig. and chiefly R.C. Church. a. A devotion in which traditionally fifteen episodes relating to the life of Christ (\"mysteries\") are contemplated, for each of which ten Hail Marys are recited, preceded by an Our Father and followed by a \"Glory be to the Father\"; (also) a book containing this (obs.); Now more commonly: a shorter form of the devotion covering a group of five of the mysteries.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "OED online, Sept. 15, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026083"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026084", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aChristmas sermons", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2015026084", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n06ffe9e2c60640c880c654d046aba303b1"}, {"@id": "_:n06ffe9e2c60640c880c654d046aba303b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Christmas sermons"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n06ffe9e2c60640c880c654d046aba303b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026107"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n06ffe9e2c60640c880c654d046aba303b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2015-09-15T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n06ffe9e2c60640c880c654d046aba303b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-10-04T14:39:31"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n06ffe9e2c60640c880c654d046aba303b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Christmas sermons"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2015026084"}
