": "en", "@value": "(Zarzuela. A Spanish genre of musical theatre characterized by a mixture of sung and spoken dialogue.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed August 11, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2016026059"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2016026060", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aBarong plays", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2016026060", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b1"}, {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Barong plays"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026341"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2016026018"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b5"}, "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b6"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Balinese dance dramas that depict the struggle between the forces of an evil witch and benign lion-like figure."}, {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2016-04-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2017-07-13T14:04:29"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Barong plays"}}, {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under South-east Asia. 6, Dance and theatre. ii, Indonesia (Balinese dance and drama, for the most part, have their origins in religious ritual and continue to serve ritual functions. Some genres involve trance possession, such as the barong and sanghyang. The barong, accompanied by a relatively large Balinese gamelan (gong kebyar or a derivative), depicts the stuggle between the forces of an evil witch (Rangda) and a benign lion-like figure (Barong), whose faithful defenders fall into trance as they attack and are repelled by the powerful Rangda)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed July 14, 2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b6", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b7"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Barong drama"}}, {"@id": "_:n02bbf4b4c48e4f5398a4db43a4b387c0b7", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Barong drama"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2016026060"}
