5651f42aebde5eb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2017-12-14T12:43:11"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Synagogue music"}}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Hoffman, B.Z. Synagogal music, 195-", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Goldstein, M. Synagogical music, 1917.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(synagogue music from the Netherlands; contents: The great feasts. Ouva schofar guadol yitakah (4:27) -- Meloch al kol haolam (3:43) -- Four schofar signals (0:45) -- Zacharti lach (4:56) -- Kol nidrei (4:11) -- Avinou malkeinou (6:40) -- Kaddisch (3:30) -- The three feasts. M\u00e9lech rachaman (3:29) -- Hodou (3:32) -- Anah (4:09) -- Sabbath. Lechra dodi (5:49) -- Adochem malach (3:39) -- Ahavat olam (2:29) -- Kiddouch (2:40) -- Kilekach tov (2:22) -- Ata yatsarta (3:20) -- Hanouccah. Hadlakat han\u00e8r (1:52) -- Han\u00e9rotchallalou (2:41) -- Maoz tsour (1:32) -- Al hanissim (4:19).)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Jewish sacred songs, 1997", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(contents: Introductory organ solo of great-festive service / arrangement by G\u00e1bor Lisznyai -- Un'sane taykef / arrangement by G\u00e1bor Lisznyai -- Emes / Salomon Sulzer -- K'vakoras / arrangement by G\u00e1bor Lisznyai -- Kaddish / traditional -- Kol nidre / traditional -- Yaale / Jakab Gottschall -- V'al y'de avodecho / arrangement by S\u00e1ndor Kov\u00e1cs, M\u00e1ria Lisznyai -- Ma tayvu / Louis Lewandowski -- V'hu rachum / arrangement by S\u00e1ndor Kov\u00e1cs, M\u00e1ria Lisznyai -- Rom v'nissoh / traditional -- V'shomru / Jakab Gottschall -- R'tse vim'nuchosenu / Jakab Gotschall -- Shaymea kay'l bichays / arrangement by S\u00e1ndor Kov\u00e1cs, M\u00e1ria Lisznyai)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Liturgy of Doh\u00e1ny Street Synagogue, Budapest, \u21171986", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(synagogue 1 a. a building for Jewish religious services and usually also for religious instruction b. (as modifier) 'synagogue services'). Derived forms: synagogical or synagogal, adjective)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Collins English dictionary online, Sept. 21, 2017", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Trio Lor\u00e1nd. Synagogical songs, 1963.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Synagogue music. UF Jewish liturgical music; Jewish religious music; Jewish sacred music; Jewish sacred vocal music. BT Jews--Music; Judaism--Liturgy; Sacred music)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, Sept. 21, 2017", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(contents: Eve of Sabbath -- Sabbath morning -- Sabbath afternoon -- Concluding service for Sabbath -- New Year's eve and morning -- Passover -- Hallel for New Moon -- Pizmon for berith -- Shochant basade -- Eve of Day of Atonement -- Morning of Day of Atonement -- Afternoon service for Day of Atonement -- Neilah -- Parashah of Bereshit -- Haftorah of Shelah Lecha -- Kinoth of the Ninth of Av)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Music of the Spanish and Portugese synagogue, \u00a91960", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "v. 1, pt. 1, p. ix (one of the great sacred musical traditions of the world; synagogal musical traditions) p. xii (synagogal choral composition; musical liturgy) p. 19 (very little extant notated synagogue music dates from before the eighteenth century) v. 1, pt. 2 (anthology of notated musical examples discussed in v. 1, pt. 1)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Kalib, S. The musical tradition of the Eastern European synagogue, 2002- :", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb14", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(synagogue music from Germany; contents: Sham'a va tismach zion / David Eisenstadt (4:01) -- Kabalat shabat. Lecha Dodi / Paul Ben-Haim (2:58) -- Mismor LeToda. Hari'u Ladonai kol HaAretz / Fromental Halevy (4:53) -- Norma. Casta diva / Vincenzo Bellini (4:40) -- Avinu Malkenu, Gebet f\u00fcr den Frieden / Lena Stein-Schneider (2:09) -- Eli, Eli / David Zehavi (2:43) -- Hadrat Kodesh / Heinrich Schalit (4:02) -- Al tashlichenu / Louis Lewandowski (3:28) -- Psalm 42, op. 42. Meine Seele d\u00fcrstet nach Gott / Felix Mendelssohn (2:51) -- Melodies for Simchat Tora (4:08) -- Shalom Aleichem (2:21) -- Shalom Aleichem / Israel Goldfarb (2:29) -- LeDor VaDor / Meir Finkelstein (3:20) -- Shehecheyonu / Meyer Machtenberg (3:13))"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cantorial highlights. 2 : revival of synagogue music in Europe, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Synagogal music"}}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Synagogal music"}}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Synagogical music"}}, {"@id": "_:ne733781ebd1c48b1805651f42aebde5eb19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Synagogical music"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2017026116"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2017026117", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMultilingual dictionaries", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2017026117", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb1"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Multilingual dictionaries"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026086"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb5"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb6"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb7"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb8"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb9"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Dictionaries that give the terms of one language in terms of one or more other languages."}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2017-12-14T12:43:11"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2017-09-30T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Multilingual dictionaries"}}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Dictionary > Kinds of dictionaries (Of all specialized dictionaries, the bilingual group are the most serviceable and frequently used. With the rise of the vernacular languages during the Renaissance, translating to and from Latin had great importance. The Welshman in England was provided with a bilingual dictionary as early as 1547, by William Salesbury. Scholars in their analyses of language, as well as practical people for everyday needs, are anxious to have bilingual dictionaries)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Britannica online, Sept. 30, 2017:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Types of dictionaries (Dictionaries can be classified into different types on the basis of several criteria: (2) The number of languages involved: monolingual, bilingual, multilingual etc.; languages dictionaries can be monolingual (or explanatory), bilingual and multilingual)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "An introduction to lexicography, via WWW, Sept. 30, 2017:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Oxford Arabic dictionary : Arabic-English \u00b7 English-Arabic, 2014.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Ratzlaff-Henriquez, B. Papiamentu/ingles dikshonario bilingual = English/Papiamentu bilingual dictionary, 2008.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n9752e5e4c2694713989e9580349a3dddb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Bilingual Dictionaries. A bilingual dictionary gives words in two languages. Each language is grouped alphabetically in separate halves of the book, with translations into the other language)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Dictionary types, via UsingEnglish.com website, Sept. 30, 2017", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2017026117"}
