f:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 486 (Lesbian and gay drama / Jill Dolan. \"Some believe this genre derives its power and definition from identity, infusing its content with preoccupations, styles, and concerns 'true' and 'authentic' to lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgendered, and/or queer communities. Other theorists and artists believe 'lesbian and gay drama' is already an archaic category, no longer necessary because such work has gradually assimilated into mainstream theatre and performance.\") p. 488 (Early overtly lesbian drama adopted experimental forms, sometimes didactic in their style and tone) p. 491 (lesbian plays of the 1980s)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "A companion to twentieth-century American drama, 2005:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd492e591d9414aad9c024f7f3714e070b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 277 (Sapphic plays in the late eighteenth century)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "DeJean, J.E. Fictions of Sappho, 1546-1937, 1989:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd492e591d9414aad9c024f7f3714e070b13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(anthology of plays; contents: Black Friday / by Alec Butler -- Growing up suites I and II and object/subject of desire / by Shawna Dempsey and Lorri Millan -- Dykes and dolls / by Lisa Lowe -- Karla and Grif / by Vivienne Laxdal -- A fertile imagination / by Susan G. Cole -- Difference of latitude / by Lisa Walter -- Swollen tongues / by Kathleen Oliver -- Life and a lover / by Natalie Meisner -- Random acts / by Diane Flacks -- Smudge / by Alex Bulmer -- Privilege / by Corrina Hodgson)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 2006411803: Lesbian plays : coming of age in Canada, \u00a92006", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd492e591d9414aad9c024f7f3714e070b14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id"