e": "en", "@value": "(collection of texts of kouta; LC subj. hdgs.: Kouta--Texts; Folk songs, Japanese--Texts) (OCoLC)62134967"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Kimura, K. Sh\u014dwa kouta, 2003-", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n591d0b8a3d624e7799642368a01ad421b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(collection of texts of kouta; LC subj. hdgs.: Kouta--Texts; Ballads, Japanese--Texts; Folk songs, Japanese--Texts)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Kouta, utazawa, hauta zensh\u016b, 1927", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026069"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026070", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aKouta", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026070", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb1"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kouta"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026811"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb5"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb6"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb7"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb8"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb10"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb13"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb16"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb19"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "For texts of kouta that appear without a musical setting see [Kouta texts.]"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-06-01T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2020-10-19T12:49:10"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kouta"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Ko-uta; one of Japanese traditional lyric song passed down through oral tradition since mid Edo period; ko-uta is classified in the utaimono (lyrical shamisen music) group like naga-uta (long song); most ko-uta may be sung in less than minute, even longer ones taking three to four minutes at most)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Ko-uta website, June 1, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 25 (kouta is perhaps the best known genre of the geisha musical repertoire; replaced utazawa as the leisure music of choice) p. 26 (during the Heian period (794-1185), the term kouta was broadly applied to court songs performed by female performers; the term was also used within the Noh tradition, and early Edo kouta incorporated the shamisen into its musical texture for odori uta (dance music) of the early Kabuki; however, these kouta should not be confused with the contemporary kouta associated with geisha, which was derived from both hauta and kiyomoto and has been called edo kouta and hayama kouta as well; first modern kouta piece was reputed to have been composed by Kiyomoto Oy\u014d in 1855)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Foreman, K.M. The gei of geisha, 2008, via Google books, viewed June 1, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(lighter forms of shamisen music, such as kouta; terms hauta (\"beginning/short songs\") and kouta (\"short songs\") were generally applied to popular songs of the period; the terms nagauta (\"long songs\") and kouta were used in earlier periods for a variety of poetic forms but eventually became specific genre names. Both terms were connected with early forms of shamisen music in the new kabuki theatre, edo nagauta eventually becoming its predominant genre)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, June 1, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(sound recording of kouta performed by Kasuga Toyo)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Kasuga, T. Kasuga Toyo kouta zensh\u016b, 1962", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 9 (a genre of music; most ko-uta may be sung in less than a minute, longer ones taking perhaps three or four at most; they are accompanied by the shamisen) p. 10 (essence is pithiness; most geisha study and perform ko-uta, and many of the songs concern male-female relations in the pleasure quarters) p. 13 (The musical structure in every case follows the text. That is, there are no \"tunes\" that exist on their own to which text would be added later) pp. 14-15 (music in early forms of Kabuki (sometime before 1650) was a type of ko-uta or ha-uta (also meaning \"short song\"); gradually the longer dance form naga-uta (\"long songs\") formed the musical backbone for Kabuki; Ko-uta and ha-uta, as emotional and sentimental small lyrics, continued to be sung in the geisha districts)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Ko-uta : \"little songs\" of the geisha world, 1979:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Edo kouta"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Edo kouta"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kouta songs"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kouta songs"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hayama kouta"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hayama kouta"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb19", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb20"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ko-uta"}}, {"@id": "_:n1751ad78fd5e438b8b422879eeaeb9dfb20", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ko-uta"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026070"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026071", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aHealth surveys", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026071", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b1"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Health surveys"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026113"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b5"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b6"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b7"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b8"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b9"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b10"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b11"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b12"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b15"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b18"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b21"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b24"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-06-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-08-03T13:39:42"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Health surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Taylor, A.W. Representative population health surveys, 2006.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Tuladhar, S. Women's empowerment and spousal violence in relation to health outcomes in Nepal : further analysis of the 2011 Nepal demographic and health surveys, 2013.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Aday, L.A. Designing and conducting health surveys, \u00a92006.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "t.p. (Health Behaviour in School-Aged Children (HBSC) Study : international report from the 2013/2014 survey) p. xii (HBSC surveys; presents data from the 2013/2014 survey) p. 2 (HBSC asks 11-, 13- and 15-year-old boys and girls about their health and well-being, social environments and health behaviours every four years using a self-report survey; data are collected in all participating countries and regions through school-based surveys)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Growing up unequal, 2016:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Health surveys. UF Public health surveys. BT Surveys)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, June 7, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Tolonen, H. Towards the high quality of population health surveys, 2006.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Integrated public health surveys, 2010-2011, 2013.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Public health"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Public health"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Population health"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Population health"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Health"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Health"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Public health surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Public health surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b24", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b25"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Population health surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nb1228167ec20441ba520d8983d6c4932b25", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Population health surveys"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026071"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026072", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aScholia", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026072", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b1"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Scholia"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026089"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b5"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b6"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b7"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b8"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b9"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b10"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b11"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b12"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b15"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Marginal notes that explain, interpret, or comment on a text, especially those added by a classical grammarian on a work by an ancient Greek or Latin author."}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2024-10-11T14:07:30"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ilchalcs"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-06-07T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Scholia"}}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(scholium: A marginal note or explanatory comment made by a scholiast)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxford dictionaries website, June 7, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "scholium (scholium, plural scholia or scholiums: 1. a marginal annotation or comment (as on the text of a classic by an early grammarian). 2. a remark or observation subjoined but not essential to a demonstration or a train of reasoning) scholion (scholion, plural scholia, also scholions: scholium)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Merriam-Webster dictionary online, June 7, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "RBMS controlled vocabularies: genre terms, via WWW, June 7, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(scholium: A marginal note explaining, interpreting, or commenting on a text, especially an annotation added by a classical grammarian on a passage from a work by Greek or Latin author of Antiquity. Plural: scholia. See also: exegesis; marginalia: marginalia Latin for \"things in the margin.\" Headings or notes printed in the margins of a page, usually in type of a size or style distinct from that of the text. Marginalia include footnotes, side notes, and shoulder notes. Also included are glosses, annotations, diagrams, doodles, etc., added by a commentator or reader. In manuscripts, corrections are sometimes made in the margins. In the case of medieval manuscripts and incunabula, the term includes notes and commentary written in the margins but not ornamental borders and other marginal decoration.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary for library and information science, June 7, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Scholia (Scholia. SA subdivision Scholia under names of individual persons. BT Criticism. BT Philology) --Scholia (--Scholia. UF --Marginalia. Use as a form subdivision under names of individual persons for marginal annotations, explanatory comments or remarks, especially on the text of a classical work by an early grammarian.) Marginalia (Marginalia. UF Marginal notes; Notes, Marginal. SN Here are entered works on notes, scribbles, or editorial comments made in the margins of books. Works on drawings and flourishes in medieval illuminated manuscript margins are entered under Marginal illustrations.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, June 7, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(scholia in Greek; LC subj. hdgs.: Aelian, active 3rd century. De natura animalium; Aelian, active 3rd century--Scholia)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Scholia in Claudii Aeliani libros De natura animalium, 2017", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Scholium: A biblical scholium may be defined as a brief exegetical explanation of a passage that is difficult on account of variant readings, obscure historical or geographical allusions, grammatical difficulties, and the like. Scholia are usually found in the margin of the text, less frequently at the foot of the page. The author as well as the collector of scholia is called a scholiast)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Encyclopedia.com, Apr. 12, 2024", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Scholions"}}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Scholions"}}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Scholiums"}}, {"@id": "_:nf8a72a9c0e8b4cc5997704b0c9a93ab6b16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Scholiums"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026072"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026073", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aSuperhero fiction", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026073", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db1"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Superhero fiction"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026333"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026529"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db5"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db6"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db7"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db8"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db9"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db10"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db11"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db12"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-06-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/mel"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-09-11T08:02:57"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Superhero fiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(After a long, close association with comics, superhero fiction is enjoying a literary heyday; the superhero novel is one of the most exciting branches of speculative fiction; other branches of speculative fiction: fantasy, science fiction, horror and magical realism)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Exploring speculative fiction sub-genres: superhero fiction, via Liminal pages website, viewed June 8, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "leaf 38 (their fantasy and science-fiction bases) leaf 325 (The superhero is a logical outgrowth of the science-fiction superman because the narrative conventions of serialized literature demand a hero-type that can be endlessly employed against symbolic representations of social \"others\") leaf 366 (Superpowers are one of the most identifiable elements of the superhero genre) leaf 371 (costume as an element of identity marked the superhero off from previous hero-types and helped to establish the genre) leaf 379 (the superhero genre as a distinct genre of its own and not an offshoot of science fiction or fantasy)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Coogan, P.M. The secret origin of the superhero : the origin and evolution of the superhero genre in America, 2002, via ProQuest dissertations & theses global, viewed June 8, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(The Side of Good / The Side of Evil, a superhero/supervillain fiction anthology)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Bellum, S. The side of good - the side of evil - flipbook anthology, via Buzzymag.com, July 22, 2015, viewed June 11, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "subtitle (an anthology of superhero fiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Path of the just, 2003:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 4 of cover (Doreen Green, age fourteen, is a little too busy wiping out crime in her suburban New Jersey neighborhood to focus on her overdue homework. That's because she also happens to be Squirrel Girl, bushy-tailed, squirrel-powered Super Hero!)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Hale, S. The unbeatable Squirrel Girl, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "pref. (superhero fiction) p. 4 of cover (Local Hero Press, LLC is a publisher of superhero and speculative fiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Caped : an anthology of superhero tales, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "cover (an anthology of science fiction & fantasy short stories and poems) foreword (superhero fiction and poetry)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Superhero universe, 2016:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Supervillain fiction"}}, {"@id": "_:n55041297d9fd40fb93e90609c69d508db13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Supervillain fiction"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026073"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026074", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aMoresche (Songs)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026074", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b1"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Moresche (Songs)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027189"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b5"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b6"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b7"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b8"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b9"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b12"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-06-08T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-12-11T13:25:26"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Moresche (Songs)"}}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Moresca, morisca: def. 2: a subgenre of the villanella caricaturing Africans or Moors)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 2003, via GoogleBooks, Aug. 2, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Moresca [morisca] (It.: 'Moorish'; Sp. morisca); (2) A carnivalesque vocal genre popular in the 16th century whose texts parody the speech of Moors, then defined broadly as Muslims or narrowly as inhabitants of the Barbary Coast. Moresche are settings of free verse in which sections in binary time alternate with dance-songs introduced by onomatopoetic imitations of instruments)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, June 8, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "title page (Villanellen und Moresken)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Lasso, O. Kompositionen mit italienischem Text, 2016:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "page 904 (Moresca; a subspecies of villanella in which singers represent Moorish girls; no relationship with the dance of the same name)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Harvard dictionary of music, 1969:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b9", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b10"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Morescas (Songs)"}}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b10", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Morescas (Songs)"}}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b12", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b13"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Moriscas (Songs)"}}, {"@id": "_:nc44e3fbe6d544b2bab04bd3e7311c728b13", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Moriscas (Songs)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026074"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026075", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aGay television programs", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026075", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b1"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Gay television programs"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026673"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b5"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b6"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b7"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b8"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b10"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Television programs featuring gay characters or addressing gay themes."}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-06-11T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2023-11-09T14:22:46"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ic"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Gay television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Terrace, V. Internet lesbian and gay television series, 1996-2014, 2015.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 1 (Gay-themed TV) p. 2 (Bravo's Queer Eye for the Straight Guy became the most talked-about show of the [2003] summer television season; gay-themed programming on U.S. network television in the 1990s)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Becker, R. Gay TV and straight America, \u00a92006:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(the most important LGBT television series of the last 45 years; LGBT TV series)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reader's poll: the 25 most important LGBT television series, via IndieWire website, Jun 15, 2014, viewed June 11, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 665 (queer television) p. 666 (LGBTQ television; LGBTQ representation on the small screen) pp. 668-669 (programs such as The L Word, which almost exclusively feature gay and lesbian characters) p. 671 (gay-themed television)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "GLQ, v. 17, no. 4 (2011):", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "container (\"Focusing on the loves, careers, ambitions and relationships of a group of gay men and women\" in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Queer as folk (Television program : U.S.). Season 1. Queer as folk. The complete first season, \u00a92001:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Homosexual television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:nddf0f9a85b944b8cb05c858d130106f4b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Homosexual television programs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026075"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026076", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aLesbian television programs", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026076", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b1"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Lesbian television programs"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026673"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b5"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b6"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b7"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b8"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b10"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Television programs featuring lesbian characters or addressing lesbian themes."}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-06-11T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2023-11-09T14:22:46"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/ic"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Lesbian television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 665 (queer television) p. 666 (LGBTQ television; LGBTQ representation on the small screen) pp. 668-669 (programs such as The L Word, which almost exclusively feature gay and lesbian characters)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "GLQ, v. 17, no. 4 (2011):", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"'Some people have wrongheaded views of the trans community or the gay community, and this show is really about seeing them as full human beings,' Ryan Murphy told Vanity Fair at the premiere of his latest drama, Pose, in New York on Thursday night. The show doesn't debut until June 3 on FX, but it's already earned headlines for its cast and crew: five trans actors, all women of color, are series regulars, and its entire team--writers, filmmakers, cast, and crew combined--includes 140 trans and L.G.B.T.Q. people.\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Chi, P. Why Ryan Murphy's new trans drama, Pose, is so personal, via Vanity fair website, posted May 18, 2018, viewed June 11, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "container (\"Focusing on the loves, careers, ambitions and relationships of a group of gay men and women\" in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Queer as folk (Television program : U.S.). Season 1. Queer as folk. The complete first season, \u00a92001:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Terrace, V. Internet lesbian and gay television series, 1996-2014, 2015.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(the most important LGBT television series of the last 45 years; LGBT TV series)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reader's poll: the 25 most important LGBT television series, via IndieWire website, Jun 15, 2014, viewed June 11, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Homosexual television programs"}}, {"@id": "_:n55e5f4db632c4b4fa6296f3e83783c52b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Homosexual television programs"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026076"}
