: "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Meadows, M.S.T. Spawning indicators of snappers (Lutjanidae) on the east coast of Florida determined from commercial and recreational fisher surveys, 2012.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(creel, or angler survey; what a creel survey amounts to is having an individual interview anglers, measure fish, keep track of hours fished, count boats, fish houses, recreational craft, etc. When the data is analyzed we can get information about the effort, harvest, size distribution of several important species of fish. We can also get an idea of fishing quality and recreational pressure a lake has been subject to)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Creel surveys, via Minnesota Dept. of Natural Resources website, July 20, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "v. 1, p. v (national survey of saltwater recreational anglers beginning in February 2013) v. 1, p. 1 (survey results)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Attitudes and preferences of saltwater recreational anglers : report from the 2013 national saltwater angler survey, 2013-2014:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 253 (Estimates of fisheries characteristics, such as effort, catch, harvest, and survival, are needed for formulating management policies in freshwater fisheries. Creel surveys are an important tool used by fisheries managers to assess these characteristics; angler creel surveys)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Alexiades, A.V. Measurement error in angler creel surveys, in North American journal of fisheries management, v. 35, issue 2 (2015), via WWW, viewed July 20, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "1992 Illinois sport fishing survey, 1994.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Graham, L. 1994 Alberta resident angling survey, 1995.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb14", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "2009376382: McCargo, J.W. Roanoke River recreational angling survey, 2005-2006, 2007.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb15", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb16"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Angling surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb16", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Angling surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Angler creel surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Angler creel surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Angler surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Angler surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb24", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb25"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Fisher"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb25", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Fisher"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb27", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb28"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Fishing"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb28", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Fishing"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb30", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb31"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Creel"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb31", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Creel"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb33", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb34"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Creel surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb34", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Creel surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb36", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb37"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Angler creel"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb37", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Angler creel"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb39", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb40"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Angling"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb40", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Surveys, Angling"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb42", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb43"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fisher surveys"}}, {"@id": "_:nebb0595b8e7244a99471ba39ebb91fedb43", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Fisher surveys"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026098"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026099", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aLight novels", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026099", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b1"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Light novels"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026339"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b5"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b6"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b7"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b8"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b9"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b10"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b11"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b14"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b17"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-07-23T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/mu"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-10-04T14:38:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Light novels"}}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 61 (Light novels. \"Light novels\" (raito noberu) comprise a new genre of young adult novels with anime- or manga-style illustrations. The term light novel often shortened to ranobe or rainobe was coined in the 1990s on a science fiction Internet forum. These prose (as opposed to graphic) novels are written with the young adult reader in mind, containing a large percentage of dialogue and the occasional reading gloss. They are often serialized in magazines, and many have been adapted for television. Popular light novel genres include romance, science fiction, fantasy, mystery and horror. Their enormous popularity among Japanese youth and young adults has led to greater numbers appearing in translation, such as Achi Taro's (1978-) Kage kara mamoru! (Next Door Ninja). See also Cell-Phone Novels)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Miller, S.J. Historical dictionary of modern Japanese literature and theater, 2009:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(English translation of a Japanese light novel) cover (Tokyo ghoul light novels book series)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: 2016058965: Towada, S. T\u014dky\u014d g\u016bru. English. Tokyo ghoul, 2016", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "([Wong is] writer of English-language light novels; the light novel runs from novella word count range to full novel length (averaging roughly 50,000 words); has a manga-style cover and monochrome illustrations at key points throughout. They are usually long, expansive series with multiple volumes--though one-shots are not unheard of; target audience is late middle-school to early adulthood; can be just as gory, profound, or racy as any other work of fiction)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wong, Melissa. In defense of the original English-language light novel, via Melissa Wong website, posted Aug. 18, 2017, viewed on July 20, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Genres > Novels > Light Novel (A light novel (or Ranobe) is a style of Japanese novel typically not more than 40-50,000 words long, usually published in bunkobon size, and are often illustrated. The text is often serialized in anthology magazines prior to collection in book form)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Goodreads website, July 20, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Light Novels; prose, written in short paragraphs for fast reading; very popular in Japan, chiefly among teenagers and young adults, but due to the amount of translation involved, very few of them make their way to English-language markets; The term light novel is a misnomer. While many people believe that the word \"light\" in the name means the novel is short (and they usually don't last much longer than 200 pages) or that it uses manga-style illustrations, the truth is that this actually refers to the text inside. Modern light novels use simpler, easier-to-read everyday kanji as opposed to \"hard\" novels, which generally contain much older words which, even for Japanese readers, may necessitate keeping a dictionary on hand to understand; Chinese-language literature has a somewhat similar phenomenon, particularly in Taiwan, though there is also a growing online force on Mainland China; much like original English language manga, there are a small group of authors writing [in English] in the style of light novels)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "TV tropes website, July 20, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(series statement: Accel world; authorized series access point: Kawahara, Reki. Akuseru w\u0101rudo (Light novel). English)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "2015049264: Kawahara, R. J\u014dka no Miko. English. Shrine maiden of the sacred fire, 2016", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b11", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b12"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rainobe"}}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b12", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Rainobe"}}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Raito noberu"}}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Raito noberu"}}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b17", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b18"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ranobe"}}, {"@id": "_:n1595bcc2c70446609f055e2794871040b18", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ranobe"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026099"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026101", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPrologues and epilogues", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026101", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb1"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Prologues and epilogues"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026415"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb5"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb6"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb7"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb8"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb9"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb10"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb11"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb12"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb13"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb16"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb19"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb22"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-10-04T14:38:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-07-27T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Prologues and epilogues"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Prologues and epilogues. UF Epilogues; Postscripts (Epilogues). RT Prefaces)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, July 27, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(prologues and epilogues of Restoration drama)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The prologues and epilogues of the Restoration, 1660-1700 : a complete edition, \u00a91981-\u00a91988", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "A collection and selection of English prologues and epilogues, 1779.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(prologues and epilogues of 18th century drama)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The prologues and epilogues of the eighteenth century : a complete edition, \u00a91990-", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Collection of prologues written for the 20 books in the Maestros modernos hispanicos series)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Mendoza, Eduardo. Qui\u00e9n se acuerda de Armando Palacio Vald\u00e9s? : escritores en lengua espa\u00f1ola : veinticuatro presentaciones y dos pr\u00f3logos, \u00a92007", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "prologue (prologue, or less commonly prolog: 1. the preface or introduction to a literary work. 2 a. a speech often in verse addressed to the audience by an actor at the beginning of a play. b. : the actor speaking such a prologue. 3. an introductory or preceding event or development) epilogue (epilogue, or less commonly epilog: 1. a concluding section that rounds out the design of a literary work. 2 a. a speech often in verse addressed to the audience by an actor at the end of a play; also : the actor speaking such an epilogue. b. the final scene of a play that comments on or summarizes the main action. 3. the concluding section of a musical composition : coda)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Merriam-Webster dictionary online, July 27, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "prologue (prologue: An introductory speech or scene given before the main play; it was during the Restoration period that the prologue, along with the closing epilogue, truly came into its own; these pieces were always in rhymed verse and often full of sharp witty comments on topical issues; John Dryden wrote numerous prologues for his own and others' plays; David Garrick was a noted writer of prologues in the 18th century) epilogue (epilogue: A brief scene, speech, or short poem at the end of a play. It often explains the moral of the drama or begs the audience's indulgence for any shortcomings)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The Methuen Drama dictionary of the theatre, 2011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "prologue (prologue: The introduction to a play, novel, poem, or other literary work placed by the author at the opening of the text, rather than in the front matter (example: The Wife of Bath's Prologue in Chaucer's The Canterbury Tales). Also refers to introductory lines spoken by a member of the cast before the beginning of the first act of a dramatic performance to prepare the audience for the theme to be developed or state the moral embodied in the action that follows. Compare with epilogue.) epilogue (epilogue: A part added as a conclusion at the close of a literary work, for example, the statement of the moral at the end of a fable. Compare with afterword. The term also refers to the final section of a speech, also called the peroration, and to a brief speech delivered at the end of a dramatic performance, requesting the approval of audience and critics. Compare in this sense with prologue.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary for library and information science, July 27, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Epilogs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Epilogs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb16", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb17"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Postscripts (Epilogues)"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb17", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Postscripts (Epilogues)"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb19", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb20"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Prologs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb20", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Prologs"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb22", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb23"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Epilogues and prologues"}}, {"@id": "_:n5b2a871602ce457e94153d1e4e4ad56fb23", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Epilogues and prologues"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026101"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026103", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aWheel charts", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026103", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb1"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Wheel charts"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026113"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb5"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb6"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb7"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb8"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb11"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb14"}], "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-10-04T14:38:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-07-29T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/gvas"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Wheel charts"}}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(volvelle also volvell, an old contrivance for ascertaining the time of the rising and setting of the moon or sun ... consisting of one or more moveable circles with pointers)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Web.3", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Volvelle (or wheel chart is a type of slide chart, a paper construction with rotating parts; volvelles that arrange their data peripherally, centrifugally, and radially; Twentieth-century volvelles--often referred to as wheel charts; \"offer everything from inventory control to color calibration, mileage metering to verb conjugation ... fortune-telling wheels and semaphore-charting wheels\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, viewed July 29, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(name not given)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Fortunescope, [1935]:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb8", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb9"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Volvelles"}}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb9", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Volvelles"}}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb11", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb12"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Volvells"}}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb12", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Volvells"}}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Charts, Wheel"}}, {"@id": "_:n8297f31086f84a0f8b964f820d039f9eb15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Charts, Wheel"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026103"}
