hecklists"}}, {"@id": "_:n5f0d6a6737044deaab2873290ac7d438b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(checklist Also check list: a list of items, as names or tasks, for comparison, verification, or other checking purposes)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Dictionary.com unabridged, Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5f0d6a6737044deaab2873290ac7d438b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(checklist : a list of things to be checked or done; also : a comprehensive list)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Merriam-Webster dictionary online, Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5f0d6a6737044deaab2873290ac7d438b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(checklist: A comprehensive list of books, periodicals, or other documents that provides the minimum amount of description or annotation necessary to identify each work--briefer than a bibliography. Also, the log kept by a library to record the receipt of each number of a serial publication or part of a work in progress. Also refers to a list of items required, or procedures to be followed, such as the steps in a library's opening or closing routine. Also spelled check-list.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Reitz, J.M. ODLIS : online dictionary for library and information science, viewed Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5f0d6a6737044deaab2873290ac7d438b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(check list: a list of items, facts, names, etc, to be checked or referred to for comparison, identification, or verification)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Collins English dictionary online, Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5f0d6a6737044deaab2873290ac7d438b9", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5f0d6a6737044deaab2873290ac7d438b10"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Check lists"}}, {"@id": "_:n5f0d6a6737044deaab2873290ac7d438b10", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Check lists"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026147"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026149", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aGraphic medicine (Comics)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026149", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b1"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic medicine (Comics)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026266"}, "madsrdf:hasEarlierEstablishedForm": {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b5"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b8"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b9"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b10"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b11"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b12"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b13"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b14"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b15"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b16"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b17"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b18"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b19"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b20"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b21"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b24"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b27"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b30"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b33"}], "madsrdf:historyNote": "[Heading changed from Medical comics to Graphic medicine (Comics) in May 2022.]", "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Comics that feature medical personnel, the practice of medicine and the experience of illness."}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-10-22T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-26T14:29:46"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/npkmc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic medicine (Comics)"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b5", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b6"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical comics"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b6", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical comics"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(comic fictional graphic novel about a breast cancer and mastectomy patient)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cazot, V. About Betty's boob, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"graphic medicine--the intersection of comics and personal narrative\"; \"the graphic novel format used for personal stories of illnesses, known as graphic medicine\"; \"the field of Graphic Medicine, focusing on the use of comics as a medium for communicating stories about medicine and the experience of illness\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Graphic medicine, via National Library of Medicine website, viewed Mar. 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Cunningham, D. Psychiatric tales : eleven graphic stories about mental illness, 2011.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"medical comics\" 42,300 results; \"graphic medicine\" 101,000 results)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Google, viewed Mar. 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"intersection between the medium of comics and the discourse of healthcare\"; term coined by Dr. Ian Williams in 2007; examples include \"graphic memoirs of illness, educational comics for both students and patients\" and other fictional and nonfiction comics related to healthcare)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Williams, I. What is \"graphic medicine\"?, via Graphic Medicine website, viewed Mar. 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(summary: \"graphic illness narratives (book-length stories about disease in the comics medium\") t.o.c. (\"graphic pathographies\") p. 99 (analyses include fictional graphic medicine narratives like \"The inflatable woman\" about a zookeeper who develops breast cancer) p. 118 (analyses also include nonfiction graphic medicine narratives like \"Our cancer year\" by Harvey Pekar and Joyce Brabner)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "El Refaie, E. Visual metaphor and embodiment in graphic illness narratives, 2019", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b14", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"comics as a resource for communicating about medicine and health\"; \"Graphic Medicine series focused on the publication of self-reflective 'graphic pathographies'\"; titles in this series include both nonfiction and fictional graphic medicine titles, like \"A thousand colored castles\" about a fictional character with Charles Bonnet syndrome)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Graphic medicine, via Penn State University Press website, viewed Mar. 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b15", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 104 (medical comics) p. 133 (healthcare comics) p. 4 of cover (graphic medicine narratives; offer patients, family members, physicians, and other caregivers new ways to experience and work with the complex challenges of the medical experience)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Czerwiec, MK. Graphic medicine manifesto, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b16", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 22 (\"graphic medicine\" as \"comics dealing with the patient experience of illness or caring for others with an illness\" and \"'comics' distinctive engagement with an performance of illness experience'\"; can be autobiographical or \"address various socio-cultural issues impinging health care such as medical negligence; the vexed doctor-patient relationship; industrialism of health care; patient identity; role of insurance providers; challenges of caretaking; demands of being a doctor in a commercialized healthcare sector, among others\"; \"graphic illness narratives\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Venkatesan, S. Rhetorics of the visual : graphic medicine, comics and its affordances, in Rupkatha journal on interdisciplinary studies in humanities, vol. 8, no. 3 (2016):", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b17", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(fictional graphic novel about a patient with cancer of the larynx)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Vanistendael, J. When David lost his voice, 2012", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b18", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"Annals Graphic Medicine brings together original graphic narratives, comics, animation/feature, and other creative forms by those who provide or receive health care. They address medically relevant topics--be they poignant, thought-provoking, or just plain entertaining;\" examples include both fictional comics like \"The Endless Battle\" and nonfiction comics like \"The Hospital Makes It Hard to Speak Up for Myself\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Annals graphic medicine, via Annals of Internal Medicine website, viewed Mar. 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b19", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "home (graphic novels on medical themes; stories invite readers to understand and empathize with patients and their caregivers) What is graphic medicine? (graphic novels, comics, and visual storytelling in medical education, patient care, and other applications related to healthcare and the life sciences; may be published in print or on the web, as a book, a series, or a single comic strip)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Graphic medicine, via Thomas Jefferson University Scott Memorial Library website, Aug. 10, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b20", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"medical comics\" 4 results; \"graphic medicine\" 267 results)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "PubMed, viewed Mar. 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic illness narratives (Comics)"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic illness narratives (Comics)"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b24", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b25"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Health care comics"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b25", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Health care comics"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b27", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b28"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical comics"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b28", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Medical comics"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b30", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b31"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic pathographies (Comics)"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b31", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic pathographies (Comics)"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b33", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b34"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Healthcare comics"}}, {"@id": "_:n688466083a0e47d68b8320a4136b68a4b34", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Healthcare comics"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026149"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026150", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aEnvironmental drama", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2018026150", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb1"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Environmental drama"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026297"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb5"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb6"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb7"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb8"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb9"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb10"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb11"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb12"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb13"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2019-02-21T10:27:35"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2018-10-22T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wau"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Environmental drama"}}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Ecodrama stages the reciprocal connection between humans and the more-than-human world. It encompasses not only works that take environmental issues as their topic, hoping to raise consciousness or press for change, but also work that explores the relation of a \"sense of place\" to identity and community)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "May, T.J. What is ecodrama?, 2007, via Earth matters on stage website, viewed Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Mills, L. Save the lofty trees : an environmental play, 2005, viewed online Oct. 22, 2018.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(plays about the environment; environmental drama can be engaging and interesting, without dumbing down or reverting to didacticism)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Butler, R. Green shoots of climate-change theatre, via The guardian website, posted 22 May 2009, viewed Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(a show about hard environmental issues in Oregon; theatre about environmental issues)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Goodbody, W. An Oregon eco fable at Salem's Pentacle Theatre, via Oregon live blog, posted June 6, 2008, viewed Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 191 (in chapter on environmental education: Drama. The students could be organised to perform short and simple environmental plays. Drama is an effective and entertaining way of putting across messages.)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Nhamo, G. Framework and tools for environmental management in Africa, 2011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(plays that not only focus on current and historic environmental issues, but also plays that enliven and transform our experience of the world around us, that inspire us to listen better, and instill a deeper or more complex sense of our ecological communities; plays that do one or more of the following: Engage the personal, local, regional and/or global implications of man-made climate change; Put an ecological issue or environmental event/crisis at the center of the dramatic action or theme of the play; Expose and illuminate issues of environmental justice; Offer an imagined world view that illuminates our ecological condition or reflects on the ecological crisis from a unique cultural or philosophical perspective; Critique or satirize patterns of exploitation, consumption, or other ingrained values that are ecologically unsustainable)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Ecodrama New Play Competition, via WWW, Oct. 22, 2018", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 136 ([Emelina Gagalac] Regis has written and staged a historical play and two environmental plays)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Santos, P.V.M., \u00a92003:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "t.p. (an eco-fable) t.p. verso (originally commissioned and produced by A Contemporary Theatre, Seattle, Washington; full-length premiere in the 1994 Humana Festival of New American Plays) p. 5 (Cast: Iko - a forest ranger; Clare Kutz - a logging contractor; Trey Hugger - founder of \"Timber Watch,\" a watchdog organization ; Terra Sawyer - an environmental activist; Russ T. Sawyer - an unemployed logger; The Creature - a yeti) p. 6 (This play is a \"fable\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: Klein, J. Betty the yeti, \u00a91995:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ecodrama"}}, {"@id": "_:ncef76a332b224620af55f5b18bf81fffb14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Ecodrama"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2018026150"}
