raphic-novel criticism) p. 204 (scholarly criticism on graphic novels) (OCoLC)1035824795"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "The Cambridge history of the graphic novel, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(OCoLC)427613097"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat.: The best American comics criticism, \u00a92010", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(OCoLC)1291008576"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "How to analyze & review comics : a handbook on comics criticism, 2021.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(title translates as: Art Spiegelman's \"Maus\" : the Holocaust in the world of comics; a work of comics criticism) (OCoLC)862208774"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Ruhnau, S. Art Spiegelmans \"Maus\" : der Holocaust in der Welt des Comics, 2013", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 4 (One structural feature of comics that literary critics remain generally in agreement over is how comics, through \"two narrative tracks, one verbal and one visual, register temporality spatially\" (Chute, \"Literature\" 452), making it a form that \"relies on space to represent time\") p. 18 (contemporary comics criticism) (OCoLC)1111292112"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Murel, J.B. Towards an aesthetics of comics : a reconsideration of comics criticism, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Books (\"You may find comics and graphic novel criticism in our book and journal article (library database) collections\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Comics and graphic novels, via Ramsey Library at UNC Asheville website, viewed Apr. 29, 2022:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab14", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(comic and graphic novel criticism)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Literature: comics/graphic novels & manga, via UW Bothell and Cascadia College Campus Library website, viewed Apr. 29, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab15", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. x (analysis of comics and graphic novels in Spain and abroad) p. xvii (Much criticism has been produced and is still being written about comics and graphic novels) (OCoLC)1015297530"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "On the edge of the panel : essays on comics criticism, 2015:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab16", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(graphic novel criticism)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Comics & graphic novels @ Cal State LA, via Cal State LA University Library website, viewed Apr. 29, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab17", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 157 (In the years that followed, a number of EC fans went on to draw or write comics for the Underground; to publish fanzines, comic criticism, and comic history; and to collect and sell comics in the emerging specialty market)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Kidman, S. Comic books incorporated, 2019, via Google books, viewed Apr. 29, 2022:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab18", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab19"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic novel criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab19", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Graphic novel criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab21", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab22"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Comic criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab22", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Comic criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab24", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab25"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Comics and graphic novel criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab25", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Comics and graphic novel criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab27", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab28"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Manga criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab28", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Manga criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab30", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab31"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Comic and graphic novel criticism"}}, {"@id": "_:n871cdecc1f824101b644b8948ce7adcab31", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Comic and graphic novel criticism"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026025"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026027", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aQaww\u0101l\u012b", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2022026027", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb1"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Qaww\u0101l\u012b"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026859"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027062"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027103"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb5"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb6"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb7"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb8"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb11"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb14"}], "madsrdf:historyNote": "[Established September 2022.]", "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-03T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-09-07T10:19:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Qaww\u0101l\u012b"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Islamic religious music. II. Sufism and popular Islam. 6. Chisht\u012b Sufism (Chisht\u012b order of Sufism; widespread in Pakistan and North India; \"Its major form, qaww\u0101l\u012b, employs texts in Persian, Urdu and other local languages such as Punjabi, often by notable poets. Performers such as the Sabri Brothers and Nusrat Fateh Ali Kh\u0101n have achieved commercial success and brought this music to a globalized and non-Muslim audience\") Pakistan, Islamic Republic of. 2. Music and Nationality. (i) Art music (semi-classical genres include Punjabi and Urdu qaww\u0101l\u012b)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, May 3, 2022:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Hindustani classical music (Qawwali; listed as a semi-classical genre of Hindustani classical music) Qawwali (\"almost all qawwalis are based on a raga from the Hindustani classical music tradition\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, May 3, 2022:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "insert, pages 9-12 (Qawwali (used as both singular and plural); Sufi musical genre; term derives from the Arabic word \"qaul\" meaning declaration or affirmation; the singer is called a qawwal; \"In essence, the qawwali is a message of peace, fraternity and love and contains no word likely to create discord\"; the performers on this album belong to the school of Hindustani music know as Qawwal Bach\u00e9) (DLC)2022619924"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Pakistan : Qawwali de la Dehli Gharana (Karachi):", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb8", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb9"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kawwali"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb9", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Kawwali"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb11", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb12"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Qawwalis"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb12", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Qawwalis"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb14", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb15"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Qawali"}}, {"@id": "_:n5d15d066080d4aedbdaaa4bfc915a0fcb15", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Qawali"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026027"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026028", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aDrone metal (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2022026028", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b1"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Drone metal (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026854"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b5"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b6"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b7"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b8"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b10"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b13"}], "madsrdf:historyNote": "[Established September 2022.]", "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-09-07T10:19:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-09T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Drone metal (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Drone metal (Cultural origins: early 1990s, Seattle, Washington)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, viewed May 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Drone metal album by psychedelic rock and metal musical group, Ryte)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Ryte, 2020:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Drone metal (\"Drone metal, also known as drone doom and power ambient, is a style of heavy metal that melds the slow tempos and heaviness of doom metal with the long-duration tones of drone music. Drone metal is sometimes associated with post-metal or experimental metal\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Metal Wiki, viewed May 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "under Drone metal (\"Drone Metal blends the slower tempos and heaviness of doom metal with longer song durations. Vocals are usually growled and screamed, and an emphasis is placed on the electric guitar. Many songs lack traditional rhythm, but create a large wall of sound, drawing comparisons to post-metal. Instrumentation featured by bands as diverse as Black Sabbath, Sleep, Swans, and Sonic Youth has had a very positive influence on the genre.Additionally, minimalist composers inspired pioneers of the genre such as Earth, Burning Witch, and Boris. Other popular bands in this genre are Sunn O))) and Teeth Of Lions Rule The Divine\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Metal music archives WWW site, viewed May 9, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Drone doom (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Drone doom (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b13", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b14"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Power ambient (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:nb89a806e2214484cab912f572fa7bda2b14", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Power ambient (Music)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026028"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026030", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aPregones (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2022026030", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b1"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Pregones (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014027009"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b5"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b6"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b7"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b8"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b9"}], "madsrdf:historyNote": "[Established September 2022.]", "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Musical works based on a street-seller's cry."}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-09T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wimtmla"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-09-07T10:19:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Pregones (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Preg\u00f3n; a Spanish word meaning announcement or street-seller's cry, has a particular meaning in both Cuban music and Latin American music in general; the use of street cries as a basis for song is particularly notable in South America and the Caribbean, where the crier is known as a pregonero. In Spain, the preg\u00f3n may include flamenco or gyspy-inspired rhythms while in Latin-America preg\u00f3n is noted for its incorporation of African rhythms such as bolero, clave, habanera and rumba. For example, the traditional preg\u00f3n from Havana \"Castillo mang\u00fc\u00e9\" is often played as a yamb\u00fa, a type of rumba)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, viewed April 25, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "side A label (preg\u00f3n)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Caserita, 1937:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Chile: Traditional music, under 6. Spanish and mestizo musics (the preg\u00f3n (street cry) ... inspired by their function and brought from Spain during the colonial period)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, viewed April 27, 2022:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 144 (Preg\u00f3n; musical genre born on the streets of the cities in Cuba where the street vendors would hawk their wares; these cries often use country melodies or traditional sones or guarachas to convey their message; popular music composers have used these street cries or pregones as the basis for their compositions)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Figueroa, Frank. Encyclopedia of Latin American music in New York, 1994:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n7c3bec772b114efdbd9e96d3424ce5f5b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Garland encyclopedia of world music, 1998", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "notfound"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026030"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026031", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aG-funk (Music)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2022026031", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b1"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "G-funk (Music)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026823"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026830"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b5"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b6"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b7"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b8"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b9"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b10"}, "madsrdf:historyNote": "[Established September 2022.]", "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-09T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wimtmla"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-09-07T10:19:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "G-funk (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Death Row (The label's first release was Dr. Dre's The Chronic in 1992, a groundbreaking album that paired explicit and often violent lyrics with commercial beats that were based on older soul, funk, and R&B songs. The musical style of The Chronic became known as \"G-Funk\" (Gangsta-funk), a style that dominated many of Death Row's early albums as well as most West Coast gangsta rap throughout the 1990s)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, May 5, 2022:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wickett Crickett. Where U from, where U from, where U from, 1996.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Dr. Dre. The chronic, 1992.", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(G-funk; short for gangsta funk, is a sub-genre of gangsta rap that emerged from the West Coast scene in the late 1980s. The genre is heavily influenced by 1970s psychedelic funk sound of artists such as Parliament-Funkadelic; G-funk (which uses funk with an artificially altered tempo) incorporates multi-layered and melodic synthesizers, slow hypnotic grooves, a deep bass, heavy use of the snare drum, background female vocals, the extensive sampling of P-Funk tunes, and a high-pitched portamento saw wave synthesizer lead. It is typically set at a tempo of anywhere between 80 to 100 BPM; although G-funk originated in Los Angeles, the subgenre drew a large amount of influence from the earlier Bay Area-based sound known as Mobb music of the mid-to-late 1980s; the majority of G-funk music has come out of California, the overall sound has been utilized by additional US rappers and hip-hop groups that were based in other states across the U.S. during the time of the style's popularity in the 1990s; Southern G-funk - in the 1990s, Houston, Texas had a small, but noteworthy g-funk scene at the peak of the genre's popularity)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Wikipedia, May 5, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 74 (One of the great commercial presences in the history of rap music has been G-funk, a style generally West Coast rap whose musical tracks tend to deploy live instrumentation, heavy on bass and keyboards, with minimal (sometimes no) sampling and often highly conventional harmonic progressions and harmonies)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Krims, Adam. Rap music and the poetics of identity:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b10", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b11"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Gangsta funk (Music)"}}, {"@id": "_:n543b7061fe0548c89b9baeb38a99a295b11", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Gangsta funk (Music)"}}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026031"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026035", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aBootlegs (Sound recordings)", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2022026035", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b1"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bootlegs (Sound recordings)"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b3"}]}, "madsrdf:exampleNote": "Note under: [Alternate takes (Sound recordings),] and [Live sound recordings.]", "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026594"}, "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b5"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b6"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b7"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b8"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b9"}], "madsrdf:historyNote": "[Established November 2022.]", "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Unofficial live sound recordings or studio recordings, usually distributed without authorization. For previously unreleased studio recordings released and distributed through normal legal channels, see [Alternate takes (Sound recordings).] For live sound recordings released and distributed through normal legal channels, see [Live sound recordings.]"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-18T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/wimtmla"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-11-14T11:32:50"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Bootlegs (Sound recordings)"}}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 125 (In the late 1960s the term \"bootlegging\" came to be used in a specialized sense. Insofar as it applied to recordings, it denoted not only the distribution of existing songs without authorization, but also the unauthorized distribution of otherwise unavailable and often newly made renditions, taken, for example, from a taped concert or broadcast, or from copies of unreleased studio sessions)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Kernfeld, B. Pop song piracy, 2011:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(hdg: Sound recordings--Pirated editions; [use for] Bootleg sound recordings)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "LCSH, July 1, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "back cover (Bootlegs are unofficial \"live\" and studio recordings of artists and bands)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Freeman, G. The bootleg guide, 2003:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Bowie, D. Ziggy in concert, 1972", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nc52ee36eb7604eeaa20bcf783c610e35b9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(Bootleg; an unauthorized copy of a recording of a concert or live broadcast. More recently the term has come to encompass recordings of rehearsals and Demo sessions. Music industry organisations distinguish between bootlegs, counterfeit recordings which are manufactured to resemble legitimate discs and tapes, and pirate copies which make no attempt to duplicate the packaging of legitimate releases. In all cases, the recordings are issued without the permission of the copyright owners of the music or the performance)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Grove music online, May 16, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}], "@id": "/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026035"}
{"@context": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/context.json", "@graph": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2022026036", "@type": ["madsrdf:Authority", "madsrdf:GenreForm"], "bflc:marcKey": "155  $aManga", "identifiers:lccn": "gf2022026036", "madsrdf:adminMetadata": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab1"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab2"}], "madsrdf:authoritativeLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Manga"}, "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab3"}]}, "madsrdf:hasBroaderAuthority": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026266"}, "madsrdf:hasNarrowerAuthority": [{"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2023026059"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2023026060"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2023026061"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2023026096"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2023026122"}, {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2024026089"}], "madsrdf:hasSource": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab5"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab6"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab7"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab8"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab9"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab10"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab11"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab12"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab13"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab14"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab15"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab16"}], "madsrdf:hasVariant": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab17"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab20"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab23"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab26"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab29"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab32"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab35"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab38"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab41"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab44"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab47"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab50"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab53"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab56"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab59"}], "madsrdf:historyNote": "[Established November 2022.]", "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSCollection": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/collection_LCGFT_General"}, "madsrdf:isMemberOfMADSScheme": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms"}, "madsrdf:note": "Comics employing a set of Japanese stylistic conventions such as black and white illustrations, right-to-left panel orientation, stylized character design with exaggerated features and expressions, dramatically shaped speech bubbles, speed lines, and onomatopoetic and exclamatory typography."}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab1", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-11-30T15:24:09"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/dlc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "revised"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab2", "@type": "ri:RecordInfo", "ri:languageOfCataloging": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/iso639-2/eng"}, "ri:recordChangeDate": {"@type": "xsd:dateTime", "@value": "2022-05-23T00:00:00"}, "ri:recordContentSource": {"@id": "http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/organizations/npkmc"}, "ri:recordStatus": "new"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab3", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab5", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(manga: \"A Japanese genre of cartoons and comic books, drawn in a meticulously detailed style, usually featuring characters with distinctive large, staring eyes\"; \"In extended use, denoting cartoons in this style from other countries\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Oxford English dictionary, viewed May 23, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab6", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(distinctive style of manga includes \"elements of character design, morphemes, or symbols and paneling\" that are \"specific to manga\" including \"people drawn with big eyes, big hair, small mouths, and pointed chins\" and a \"unique distribution of panel transitions\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Kaczuk, Z. Re-examining the \"What is manga\" problematic. Arts, vol. 7, no. 3 (Sept. 2018), viewed May 23, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab7", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(an OEL manga by Chinese-Australian author Queenie Chan, published by Tokyopop) OCoLC(606763915)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Chan, Q. The dreaming : the collection, 2010", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab8", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(manga \"usually used in reference to Japanese comics characterized by a set of stylistic conventions that evolved in the postwar period. These include exaggerated physical features such as large eyes, big hair and elongated limbs; right-to-left panel sequencing; and dramatically shaped speech bubbles, speed lines and onomatopoetic, exclamatory typography\"; \"origins as a fusion of ukiyo-e (traditional woodblock prints) and Western forms of sequential art\"; \"more and more manga is now being created outside of Japan--and by non-Japanese artists,\" including \"Warcraft\" which is \"written by an American and illustrated by a Korean, and Fred Gallagher's 'Megatokyo'\"; \"publishers like Tokyopop are bringing out titles in manga style by non-Japanese artists\"; \"manga-style stories\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Webb, M. Manga by any other name is... : do Japan's world-conquering cartoons have to be created by Japanese to be the real deal?, May 28, 2006, via Wayback machine, viewed May 17, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab9", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(a long-running manga series from VIZ Media; series title \"Shonen Jump manga\") OCoLC(1272600321)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Work cat: Horikoshi, K. My hero academia. 19, School festival, 2019", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab10", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 596 (Manga: \"Use for individual works, collections, or materials about manga\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Sears list of subject headings, 22nd edition, 2018:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab11", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "p. 11 (\"The vast majority of manga published in Japan are, in the strictest sense, what is known as story manga. Story manga tell a continuous story over a large number of pages\"; \"the word 'manga' is typically used by English speakers to refer to exclusively Japanese story manga. Moverover, it connotes certain stereotypes about specific types of narrative and artistic content\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Brienza, C. Manga in America, 2016:", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab12", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(summary: \"blends traditional Haida imagery with Japanese manga\") OCoLC(994056253)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Yahgulanaas, M. Red : a Haida manga, 2014", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab13", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"Manga (Comic books)\", in hierarchy of \"Comics by form\"; \"often produced in black and white, with the cover or the first few pages in color, with emphasis on exaggerated facial expressions and large eyes\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Art and architecture thesaurus, viewed May 17, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab14", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"Use subjects beginning 'COMICS & GRAPHIC NOVELS / Manga' for works initially published in Asian territories, or for works published in the style of such Asian works\"; vocabulary contains 21 terms for types of manga)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "BISAC Subject Headings List, Comics and Graphic Novels, viewed May 17, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab15", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(\"an original English-language manga or OEL manga is a comic book or graphic novel drawn in the style of manga and originally published in English\"; \"international manga\" is also a term used to describe \"manga-inspired comics\" in various languages and from various countries outside Japan; \"Original English-language manga first began to appear in the U.S. in the mid-1980s\"; sometimes also called \"American manga\" and shortened to \"Amerimanga\"; \"Other variations on OEL manga, such as western manga, world manga, global manga, manga-influenced comics, neo-manga, and nissei comi can occasionally be heard as substitute names, but the term OEL manga is most commonly used today\")"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Original English-language manga, via Wikipedia, viewed May 17, 2022", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab16", "@type": "madsrdf:Source", "madsrdf:citationNote": {"@language": "en", "@value": "(a manga series from Kodansha Comics) OCoLC(1310477231)"}, "madsrdf:citationSource": "Nogiri, Y. Love in focus. Volume 1, 2019", "madsrdf:citationStatus": "found"}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab17", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab18"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Western manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab18", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Western manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab20", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab21"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "OEL manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab21", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "OEL manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab23", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab24"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "International manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab24", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "International manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab26", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab27"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Manga-inspired comics"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab27", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Manga-inspired comics"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab29", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab30"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Amerimanga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab30", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Amerimanga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab32", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab33"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "American manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab33", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "American manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab35", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab36"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Story manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab36", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Story manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab38", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab39"}]}, "madsrdf:variantLabel": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Original English-language manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab39", "@type": "madsrdf:GenreFormElement", "madsrdf:elementValue": {"@language": "en", "@value": "Original English-language manga"}}, {"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab41", "@type": ["madsrdf:GenreForm", "madsrdf:Variant"], "madsrdf:elementList": {"@list": [{"@id": "_:nd55e11034563482b98d67850939e4bbab42"}]}, "madsrdf:v